/* Question bank PA test (English convenience translation), Wft Pensions. Vorm: [vraag, [[antwoord, uitleg] x4], toetsterm CDFD]; het EERSTE antwoord is steeds het juiste.
   Gegenereerd met tools/vragen-js.py. */
(window.PA_VRAGEN = window.PA_VRAGEN || {})["pensioen"] = [
["What three pillars make up the Dutch pension system?", [["AOW (state pension), occupational pensions and individual supplements", "The first pillar is the AOW, the second is the pension through the employer and the third is individual provision such as an annuity (lijfrente)."], ["AOW, Anw (Surviving Dependants Act) and occupational pension", "The Anw is a survivor's benefit within social security and not a separate pension pillar."], ["Occupational pension, annuity (lijfrente) and equity in the owner-occupied home", "The owner-occupied home can help financially after retirement, but it is not a pension pillar."], ["AOW, social assistance and individual supplements", "Social assistance is a safety net under the Participation Act and is not part of the pension pillars."]], "1h.3"],
["Which pillar does an annuity policy (lijfrenteverzekering) belong to if a self-employed person without staff takes it out themselves?", [["The third pillar", "Individual provision arranged on one's own initiative, such as annuities (lijfrente) and bank savings for retirement (banksparen), forms the third pillar."], ["The first pillar", "The first pillar is the AOW, a national insurance scheme that is not built up through individual choice."], ["The second pillar", "The second pillar is the pension built up through the employer or a mandatory occupational scheme."], ["The zeroth pillar", "The term 'zeroth pillar' is sometimes used informally, but an individual annuity falls within the third pillar."]], "1h.3"],
["How is the AOW mainly financed?", [["Through a pay-as-you-go system: working people pay for current AOW recipients, topped up by a government contribution", "Today's AOW premiums finance today's benefits; because the premiums are not sufficient, the State tops up the shortfall from tax revenue."], ["Through funding: every insured person saves their own AOW capital with the SVB (Dutch Social Insurance Bank) from the age of 17", "Funding belongs to the second and third pillars; no individual capital is built up for the AOW."], ["Through premiums that employers and employees pay to an industry-wide pension fund, which pays out the AOW", "Industry-wide pension funds provide second-pillar pensions, not the AOW."], ["Entirely from the returns on the SVB's pension assets", "The SVB administers the AOW but does not manage pension assets from which the AOW is paid."]], "1h.3"],
["What is a characteristic difference between the second and the third pillar?", [["The second pillar runs via employer or occupational group, the third rests on individual choice", "Occupational pension is linked to the employment relationship; third-pillar products are taken out by the individual."], ["The second pillar is always voluntary, the third pillar is mandatory by law", "It is rather the other way round: participation in an employer's scheme is often mandatory, the third pillar is voluntary."], ["The second pillar is administered by the SVB, the third pillar by the UWV (Employee Insurance Agency)", "The SVB administers the AOW and the UWV the employee insurance schemes; pension providers administer the second pillar."], ["No tax is ever levied on the second pillar, while the third pillar is always taxed in box 1 on payout", "For both pillars the reverse-taxation rule (omkeerregel) generally applies: contributions are deductible or exempt, benefits are taxed."]], "1h.3"],
["Insurers and other financial parties sometimes make agreements among themselves about how they work, for example in a covenant or a code of conduct. What is the characteristic difference between such self-regulation and laws and regulations?", [["Self-regulation consists of agreements made by the sector itself that have not been imposed by the legislator", "With self-regulation, parties set their own standards; compliance runs through the sector and the agreements, not through the law."], ["Self-regulation only applies after approval by the House of Representatives and then has the force of law", "Self-regulation is not enacted by parliament; otherwise it would be legislation."], ["Self-regulation replaces the law: anyone who complies with a covenant does not have to comply with the Pensions Act", "Self-regulation exists alongside the law and releases no one from legal obligations."], ["Self-regulation only applies to consumers, legislation only to employers", "The difference lies in who sets the rules, not in whom they apply to."]], "1a.2"],
["In which act are the tasks and powers of DNB (De Nederlandsche Bank) and the AFM (Netherlands Authority for the Financial Markets) in the supervision of pension funds primarily laid down?", [["In the Pensions Act", "The Pensions Act regulates the supervision of pension funds by DNB and the AFM."], ["In the Financial Supervision Act (Wft)", "The Wft regulates the supervision of, among others, insurers, PPIs (premium pension institutions) and advisers, but the supervision of pension funds is laid down in the Pensions Act."], ["In the General Old Age Pensions Act (AOW)", "The AOW regulates the first-pillar old-age pension, not the supervision of pension funds."], ["In the Works Councils Act (WOR)", "The WOR regulates employee participation in companies, not the supervision of pension funds."]], "1a.4"],
["Over what period does a person build up AOW?", [["The 50 years immediately preceding their own AOW age", "The accrual period moves along with the AOW age and begins 50 years before that age."], ["From the 15th birthday up to the AOW age", "A fixed starting age of 15 no longer applies since the AOW age began to move with life expectancy."], ["From the first working day up to the AOW age", "AOW accrual is based on living or working in the Netherlands, not on the first working day."], ["The 40 years immediately preceding their own AOW age, counted per calendar year", "The period is 50 years; 40 years would yield only 80%."]], "1h.3"],
["Fatima is 52 and came to the Netherlands at the age of 30 from a country outside Europe. Before that she was never insured for the AOW. Since then she has lived and worked in the Netherlands without interruption and will continue to do so. Assume an AOW age of 67, so that the accrual period begins at her 17th birthday. What percentage of the full AOW does Fatima build up?", [["74%", "She misses the 13 years from age 17 to age 30; 37 insured years times 2% gives 74%."], ["80%", "This would apply with 40 insured years; Fatima has 37 years."], ["70%", "This would apply with 35 insured years, but she is insured for 37 years."], ["100%", "A full AOW requires 50 insured years; Fatima misses the years before her arrival."]], "1h.14"],
["How is the AOW age linked to life expectancy?", [["The AOW age rises by two thirds of the increase in life expectancy and is set five years in advance", "Since the 2019 act, one extra year of life expectancy counts for eight months, and the age is announced five years beforehand."], ["The AOW age rises one-to-one with the increase in life expectancy and is adjusted immediately every year by the SVB", "A one-to-one link applied earlier; it is now two thirds, with a notice period of five years."], ["The AOW age is fixed by law at 67 and is no longer adjusted", "After 2024 the AOW age can rise further through the link with life expectancy."], ["The AOW age is agreed per collective labour agreement (cao) between employers and trade unions", "The AOW age is regulated by law; cao parties only deal with the employer's pension scheme."]], "1h.13"],
["What is the level of the AOW benefit linked to?", [["To the net minimum wage", "The AOW follows the net minimum wage; different percentages of it apply to a single person and to people living together."], ["To the last-earned salary of the AOW recipient", "The AOW is not income-dependent; one's own salary plays no role."], ["To the funding ratio of the pension funds", "The funding ratio matters for second-pillar pensions, not for the AOW."], ["To the average salary over the whole career", "An average-salary basis is found in employer schemes, not in the AOW."]], "1h.3"],
["A logistics company is taken over by a larger transport company. All 40 employees, including planner Youssef (34), transfer to the new employer. The old employer had a pension scheme with an insurer. The new employer already offers its own staff a different pension scheme and wants to use it for the new colleagues as well. Youssef asks whether his old pension scheme simply continues. What is correct in this transfer of undertaking?", [["His terms of employment transfer, but pension is an exception if the new employer offers its own scheme", "In a transfer of undertaking, the rights under the employment contract transfer; the pension scheme does not if the acquirer itself offers the employees a pension scheme."], ["The new employer must always continue the old pension scheme unchanged, like all of Youssef's other terms of employment", "For pension, the transfer of undertaking provides an exception."], ["In a transfer of undertaking all employment contracts end and Youssef has to apply for a job again", "Employment contracts transfer by operation of law in a transfer of undertaking."], ["Youssef has to cash in his accrued pension on the transfer because the old scheme stops", "The pension already accrued remains as a paid-up entitlement or can be transferred; cashing in is in principle not permitted."]], "1b.6"],
["Do the assets or other income of an AOW recipient play a role in the level of the AOW?", [["No, the AOW is a national insurance scheme without an income or asset test", "The level depends on the number of insured years and the living situation, not on income or assets."], ["Yes, if assets exceed the social assistance asset limit, the AOW is reduced proportionally", "An asset test exists for social assistance, not for the AOW."], ["Yes, an occupational pension is offset against the AOW", "The AOW is not offset against an occupational pension; the employer's scheme does, however, often take the AOW into account through the offset (franchise)."], ["Only the partner's income is taken into account", "The partner's income does not affect the AOW; only the living situation (single or living together) counts."]], "1h.3"],
["What is meant by the Anw gap (Anw-hiaat)?", [["The income gap on death because the Anw pays nothing or only limited benefits and the partner's pension does not cover this", "Owing to the strict conditions and the income test of the Anw, a surviving dependant may fall short of income; that gap is called the Anw gap."], ["The difference between the AOW for single persons and for people living together", "That difference has nothing to do with the Anw; it concerns the AOW living situation."], ["The period between the end of the WW (unemployment) benefit and the start date of the AOW, in which only social assistance is possible", "That is an unemployment gap; the Anw gap concerns the death of a partner."], ["The shortfall in AOW accrual due to years abroad", "That is an AOW gap due to missing insured years, not an Anw gap."]], "1c.11"],
["How can the Anw gap be covered?", [["With an Anw gap insurance or pension, often through the pension provider, or with a term life insurance", "These provisions pay out on the death of the partner and thus top up the missing income."], ["With an application for voluntary AOW insurance with the SVB, which pays an Anw supplement on death", "Voluntary AOW insurance fills AOW gaps, not the loss of income on death."], ["With a high-low construction in the old-age pension, whereby the partner receives a higher benefit even before the retirement date", "A high-low construction determines the level of one's own old-age pension and does not cover the risk of death."], ["With a WW (unemployment) benefit for the surviving dependant", "The death of a partner gives no entitlement to WW; WW concerns unemployment."]], "1i.8"],
["Sanne is 38 and lived together unmarried with Tim, with whom she had a cohabitation agreement. They have no children. Sanne works full time as a nurse and is not incapacitated for work. Tim dies unexpectedly of cardiac arrest. Is Sanne entitled to an Anw survivor's benefit?", [["No: she has no child under 18, is not at least 45% incapacitated for work and was not born before 1950", "For the Anw, a surviving dependant must meet one of these entry conditions; Sanne meets none of them."], ["Yes, because anyone who ran a joint household with the deceased is entitled to an Anw benefit", "A joint household is indeed necessary, but one of the entry conditions must also be met."], ["No, because unmarried cohabitants never fall under the Anw, even with a cohabitation agreement", "Unmarried cohabitants with a joint household can fall under the Anw."], ["Yes, but only during the first year after the death, as a bridging benefit from the SVB", "Such a general one-year bridging benefit does not exist under the Anw."]], "1h.16"],
["When does an Anw survivor's benefit end in any case?", [["On reaching the AOW age", "From the AOW age the surviving dependant is entitled to AOW and the Anw benefit stops."], ["After exactly five years of benefit", "The Anw has no fixed maximum duration of five years."], ["As soon as the surviving dependant turns 50", "The age of 50 is not a cut-off point for the Anw."], ["On the surviving dependant's first pay rise", "Income can reduce the benefit through the income test, but a pay rise does not automatically end the entitlement."]], "1h.16"],
["What is the difference between partner's pension on an accrual basis and on a risk basis?", [["With the accrual basis the entitlement remains after leaving employment; with the risk basis there is cover only during participation (plus any run-off)", "The risk basis works like a term life insurance: nothing is built up that remains after participation ends."], ["With the risk basis a higher capital is built up than with the accrual basis, which passes to the new provider on leaving employment through value transfer", "With the risk basis no capital is built up; the premium only pays for the cover."], ["With the accrual basis the cover is valid only after ten years of participation; with the risk basis immediately from the first working day", "With the accrual basis the entitlement grows per year of participation; there is no ten-year waiting period."], ["There is no difference; they are two names for the same thing", "The difference is substantial, especially on changing jobs: on a risk basis the cover can lapse."]], "1i.6"],
["Pieter (41) works as a fitter at an installation company and has a partner's pension on a risk basis there. He lives with Eva and they have a son aged 6. Pieter resigns and continues as a self-employed person without staff (zzp'er). He assumes that Eva will receive his old employer's partner's pension on his death. What should the adviser point out to Pieter?", [["That the partner's pension cover lapses after any run-off period and he must arrange his own death risk cover", "On a risk basis the cover ends with participation; as a zzp'er he must cover the survivor risk himself, for example with a term life insurance."], ["That Eva keeps the full partner's pension for life, even if he pays no premium at all after his resignation", "With a risk basis no entitlement remains after participation ends."], ["That the partner's pension passes automatically to the Anw, which gives Eva a supplement on his death", "The Anw is a separate national insurance scheme with its own conditions and does not take over the partner's pension."], ["That he can have the partner's pension cashed in on leaving employment and pay the amount into an annuity (lijfrente)", "With a risk basis there is no accrued value that can be cashed in."]], "1c.11"],
["What does exchanging partner's pension for old-age pension involve?", [["The participant exchanges (part of) the partner's pension for a higher old-age pension, with the partner's written consent", "Because the partner loses their entitlement, the Pensions Act requires that partner's written consent."], ["The partner exchanges their own old-age pension for a higher partner's pension on the death of the participant", "Exchange concerns the rights within the participant's scheme, not the partner's own pension."], ["The participant exchanges partner's pension for a higher old-age pension without involving the partner, provided they report this before the retirement date", "Precisely because the partner loses rights, their written consent is required."], ["The employer unilaterally decides to convert the partner's pension", "Exchange is a right of choice of the participant, with the partner's consent, not an employer decision."]], "1g.13"],
["What is the purpose of an orphan's pension?", [["A benefit for the children of a deceased participant up to an age determined in the scheme", "The orphan's pension supports children financially after the death of the parent who was a participant."], ["A lifelong benefit for the children of a participant, starting on the participant's retirement date", "The orphan's pension is temporary and ends at the age determined by the scheme."], ["A supplement to child benefit as long as the participant is alive", "The orphan's pension only pays out after the participant's death."], ["A benefit for the participant's ex-partner after divorce", "An ex-partner's rights run through pension equalisation (verevening) and the special partner's pension, not through the orphan's pension."]], "1i.5"],
["Who counts as a partner for the partner's pension of an unmarried cohabiting participant?", [["That is determined by the pension regulations; a cohabitation agreement or registration with the provider is often required", "Married persons and registered partners are normally partners automatically; for cohabitants the scheme sets its own conditions."], ["Anyone registered at the same address in the BRP (municipal personal records database) for at least six months, regardless of the regulations", "Registration at the same address alone is usually not sufficient; the scheme determines the conditions."], ["Unmarried cohabitants can never receive a partner's pension", "Many schemes do provide partner's pension for cohabitants, provided the conditions are met."], ["Only a partner with whom the participant has children, provided parenthood is legally recognised", "Children are not a general condition for the partner concept in pension schemes."]], "1i.5"],
["To which pension does the standard equalisation of the Pensions (Division on Divorce) Act (Wvps) apply on divorce?", [["The old-age pension accrued during the marriage or registered partnership", "Only the accrual during the marriage period is equalised; accrual before or after is not."], ["All the old-age pension the participant has ever accrued, including before the marriage", "Accrual from before the marriage and after the divorce falls outside the equalisation."], ["The AOW of both ex-partners", "The AOW is a personal right and is not equalised."], ["The partner's pension accrued during the marriage", "The accrued partner's pension is not equalised; for that the ex-partner receives the special partner's pension."]], "1h.18"],
["What is the special partner's pension (bijzonder partnerpensioen)?", [["The partner's pension accrued up to the divorce that remains intended for the ex-partner after the divorce", "On divorce the ex-partner retains a right to the partner's pension accrued up to that point."], ["An additional partner's pension that the provider grants after the divorce to a new partner of the participant", "A new partner receives at most partner's pension on later accrual; the special partner's pension is for the ex-partner."], ["A temporary partner's pension until the partner's AOW age", "The special partner's pension is not temporary by definition and is not linked to the partner's AOW age."], ["The part of the old-age pension that the ex-partner receives through equalisation", "The equalised old-age pension and the special partner's pension are two different rights."]], "1h.18"],
["What is the difference between equalisation (verevening) and conversion (conversie) on divorce?", [["With conversion the ex-partner receives an independent pension right; with equalisation the payment remains dependent on the participant's life", "With conversion the rights are split definitively; with equalisation, payment to the ex-partner in principle stops when the participant dies."], ["Conversion is the statutory default on divorce; equalisation must be agreed separately in prenuptial terms or a divorce covenant", "It is the other way round: equalisation is the default, and for conversion both ex-partners and the provider must cooperate."], ["With equalisation the pension is cashed in and paid out immediately; with conversion it is only split on the retirement date", "Equalisation leads to a periodic benefit from the retirement date, not to cashing in."], ["There is no difference; both terms stand for equal division", "Both concern division, but the difference in the independence of the right is substantial."]], "1h.18"],
["Mark and Lotte divorced after twelve years of marriage. In those years Mark accrued old-age pension at his employer's pension fund. In the hustle around the divorce they left the form for the pension provider lying around. Only three years after the registration of the divorce do they report it to the fund after all. What is the consequence of this for Lotte?", [["The provider does not have to pay her directly; she must obtain her share from Mark herself", "After the two-year reporting period Lotte retains her right to equalisation, but against Mark and no longer directly against the provider."], ["Lotte loses all right to equalisation because the statutory two-year reporting period has expired", "The right to equalisation remains; only direct payment by the provider lapses."], ["The provider still equalises automatically and directly, because no statutory period applies to the report", "A two-year period does apply for direct payment by the provider."], ["Mark must pay the provider a fine for the late report", "The law provides no fine for a late report; the consequence lies in the way of payment."]], "1h.18"],
["Esther (45) and Ruud (47) lived together unmarried for fifteen years. They had a cohabitation agreement, but no marriage or registered partnership. In those years Ruud accrued a substantial old-age pension at his employer; Esther worked part time and accrued little. Now they are separating. Does the Pensions (Division on Divorce) Act (Wvps) apply to Ruud's pension?", [["No, the Wvps applies only to marriage or registered partnership; division can be done through their own agreements", "Unmarried cohabitants do not fall under the Wvps; they can, however, agree a division in their cohabitation agreement."], ["Yes, the Wvps applies to anyone who ran a joint household and was registered at the same address", "The Wvps is linked to marriage and registered partnership, not to cohabitation."], ["Yes, but only if they have children together", "Having children does not make the Wvps applicable."], ["Yes, because they lived together for more than five years and had a cohabitation agreement", "The duration of cohabitation or a cohabitation agreement does not make the Wvps applicable."]], "1h.18"],
["Can spouses deviate from the standard equalisation of the Wvps?", [["Yes, through prenuptial terms or a divorce covenant they can divide differently or exclude equalisation", "The Wvps is the default, but the parties can agree otherwise in writing."], ["No, equal division is mandatory law; only the court can deviate from it in the divorce ruling", "Deviation is possible through prenuptial terms or a covenant."], ["Only with the permission of De Nederlandsche Bank", "DNB supervises providers and does not decide on agreements between ex-partners."], ["Only if the pension provider itself decides to", "The agreement lies with the spouses themselves; the provider carries out their choice."]], "1h.18"],
["Between which parties is the pension agreement concluded?", [["Between the employer and the employee", "The pension agreement is the arrangement on pension as part of the terms of employment."], ["Between the employer and the pension provider", "That is the implementation agreement, not the pension agreement."], ["Between the employee and the pension provider", "The relationship between provider and employee is laid down in the pension regulations."], ["Between the employee and De Nederlandsche Bank", "DNB is a supervisor and not a party to a pension agreement."]], "1i.1"],
["What is the agreement between the employer and the pension provider on the implementation of the pension scheme called?", [["The implementation agreement", "In it the employer and provider lay down, among other things, how the premium is paid and what information is exchanged."], ["The pension regulations", "The pension regulations describe the rights and obligations between provider and participant."], ["The pension agreement", "The pension agreement is concluded by the employer with the employee."], ["The implementation regulations (uitvoeringsreglement)", "Implementation regulations are used for mandatory participation in an industry-wide pension fund, but the general term is implementation agreement."]], "1i.1"],
["What does the obligation to place pension (onderbrengingsplicht) in the Pensions Act entail?", [["The employer must place the pension agreement with a pension fund, pension insurer or PPI (premium pension institution)", "In this way the pension assets are separate from the risk of the company."], ["The employer must offer every employee a pension scheme", "The Pensions Act does not oblige anyone to offer pension; an obligation can, however, arise from a collective labour agreement (cao) or mandatory participation."], ["The employee must place their pension with an insurer themselves", "The obligation rests on the employer, not on the employee."], ["The employer must put the pension assets in a blocked bank account of the company, separate from working capital", "Keeping pension assets within the company itself is precisely not permitted for employees."]], "1g.8"],
["Is an employer legally obliged to offer their employees a pension scheme?", [["No, unless mandatory participation in an industry-wide pension fund or a collective labour agreement (cao) obliges them to", "The Pensions Act regulates what applies if there is a pension scheme, but contains no general obligation to offer one."], ["Yes, every employer with staff must offer pension", "A general pension obligation for employers does not exist in the Netherlands."], ["Yes, but only for employees with a permanent contract", "Even for permanent employees there is no general legal obligation."], ["No, and an employer cannot be obliged through mandatory participation in an industry-wide pension fund either", "Through mandatory participation, participation in an industry-wide pension fund can indeed be compulsory."]], "1g.8"],
["Which description fits a defined benefit agreement (uitkeringsovereenkomst)?", [["The employer promises a certain pension benefit, for example on an average-salary basis", "In a defined benefit agreement the level of the benefit is central and the required premium is variable."], ["The employer promises a fixed premium and the benefit depends on the return", "That is a defined contribution agreement (premieovereenkomst)."], ["The employer promises a fixed capital on the retirement date with which a benefit is purchased", "That is a defined capital agreement (kapitaalovereenkomst)."], ["The employee decides each year how much premium the employer pays", "None of the statutory pension agreements works like that."]], "1h.2"],
["What characterises a defined capital agreement (kapitaalovereenkomst)?", [["A fixed capital is promised on the retirement date, with which a benefit is purchased", "The capital is fixed; the level of the benefit depends on the annuity purchase rates at that time."], ["A fixed lifelong benefit is promised", "A promised benefit belongs to the defined benefit agreement."], ["Only a fixed premium is promised, without any guarantee", "That is characteristic of the defined contribution agreement."], ["A fixed capital is promised that is paid out on the retirement date as a freely withdrawable lump sum", "The capital must be converted into a pension benefit and is not freely withdrawable."]], "1h.3"],
["In which pension agreement does the investment risk in principle lie with the participant?", [["In the defined contribution agreement (premieovereenkomst)", "The employer pays an agreed premium; the final benefit depends on the investment result."], ["In the defined benefit agreement", "There a benefit is promised and the risk lies mainly with the provider and the collective."], ["In the defined capital agreement", "The capital is fixed; the investment risk during accrual does not lie with the participant."], ["In none of the agreements; that risk always lies with the employer", "In a defined contribution agreement the employer precisely does not bear the investment risk."]], "1f.2"],
["What is value transfer (waardeoverdracht)?", [["Taking the value of accrued pension entitlements to the new employer's provider", "In this way the former participant can consolidate their pension with the new employer's provider."], ["Transferring pension to the ex-partner after divorce", "Division on divorce runs through equalisation or conversion, not through value transfer."], ["Paying out the value of the pension as a lump sum on leaving employment, on which wage tax is withheld", "That is cashing in (afkoop); with value transfer the money remains intended for pension."], ["Converting pension into an annuity (lijfrente) at a bank", "Value transfer goes to the new employer's pension provider, not to a bank annuity."]], "1h.4"],
["When is individual value transfer temporarily not permitted?", [["When the funding ratio of the transferring or the receiving pension provider is below 100%", "This prevents a shortfall from being taken along or those left behind from being disadvantaged."], ["When the employee has worked for less than ten years for the old employer and so has no unconditional entitlement yet", "There is no minimum period of service of ten years for value transfer."], ["When the new employer is active in a different industry", "A different industry is no ground for refusing value transfer."], ["When the employee is older than 55", "There is no age limit of 55 for value transfer."]], "1h.4"],
["What is the purpose of the rules on automatic value transfer of small pensions?", [["To prevent participants from keeping many small, fragmented pensions with different providers", "Small pensions are thus consolidated with the new employer's provider, so that they are not lost or cashed in."], ["To pay out small pensions in cash immediately on leaving employment, so that the participant can dispose of them", "The arrangement is precisely intended to preserve small pensions for old age."], ["To transfer small pensions to the AOW", "Second-pillar pension cannot be transferred to the AOW."], ["To have small pensions converted into an annuity (lijfrente) in the employer's name", "A pension is not converted into an annuity in the employer's name."]], "1g.4"],
["What requirements must pension information meet at least under the Pensions Act?", [["Correct, clear and balanced", "The information must also be comprehensible and timely, so that the participant can base a decision on it."], ["Complete, legal and exhaustive", "Exhaustive legal information comes precisely at the expense of comprehensibility."], ["Exclusively in writing and on paper", "Pension information may also be provided electronically."], ["Approved in advance by the AFM", "The AFM supervises pension communication, but does not approve information in advance."]], "2a.5"],
["What is the Uniform Pension Overview (UPO) for an active participant?", [["A periodic overview from the provider of accrued and attainable pension entitlements in a fixed format", "Because all providers follow the same format, overviews can be compared with one another."], ["An overview that the adviser is obliged to prepare for every pension advice and send to the client annually", "The UPO comes from the pension provider, not from the adviser."], ["An annual overview from the SVB with the AOW only", "The SVB provides information about the AOW; the UPO concerns the pension with the provider."], ["A contract in which the employee records their choices", "The UPO is an information overview, not a contract."]], "1g.13"],
["Kees (44) worked for nine years as a logistics employee at a wholesaler and accrued pension at that industry's pension fund. Last year he moved to an online shop with its own pension scheme with an insurer. He did not have his old pension transferred, so a paid-up entitlement remains at the old fund. Kees asks how he is now known at that fund. What is correct?", [["As a former participant (gewezen deelnemer)", "A former participant has left a paid-up entitlement with the provider when participation ended."], ["As a pensioner (pensioengerechtigde)", "A pensioner already receives a pension benefit; Kees has not retired yet."], ["As a prospective participant (aspirant-deelnemer)", "A prospective participant has yet to start participating; Kees has precisely already participated."], ["As an active participant (actieve deelnemer)", "Kees no longer accrues anything at the old fund, so he is no longer an active participant there."]], "1h.3"],
["Which two types of contribution schemes does the Pension Transition Act (Wtp) provide for?", [["The solidarity contribution scheme and the flexible contribution scheme", "In the new system pensions are built up in one of these two schemes."], ["The average-salary scheme and the final-salary scheme", "These are variants of the defined benefit agreement that disappear in the new system."], ["The capital scheme and the new-style defined contribution scheme", "These terms belong to the old system and are not the two new Wtp contracts."], ["The collective scheme and the bank scheme", "A 'bank scheme' does not exist as a contract form under the Wtp."]], "1h.13"],
["What is a characteristic of the solidarity contribution scheme?", [["Investment is collective, with a solidarity reserve to cushion shocks and share risks", "Returns are allocated to age groups under fixed rules; the solidarity reserve provides additional risk sharing."], ["Each participant chooses their own investment mix and bears the full risk, without a collective reserve", "That fits the flexible contribution scheme better."], ["The benefit is guaranteed by the employer", "In the solidarity contribution scheme no benefit is guaranteed; there is a pension ambition."], ["There is no investing; the pension grows only with the premiums", "In the solidarity contribution scheme too, assets are invested."]], "1f.3"],
["What is a characteristic of the flexible contribution scheme?", [["The participant has their own pension assets, invested according to a lifecycle, with choice options", "The risk is aligned with the participant's age and risk profile."], ["All participants share one collective pool of assets without personal allocation, with a solidarity reserve for shocks", "In both Wtp schemes the participant has personal pension assets."], ["The employer chooses the level of the benefit anew each year", "The benefit depends on the accrued assets, not on an annual employer choice."], ["The participant may freely withdraw the assets at any time", "Pension assets remain intended for pension and cannot be freely withdrawn."]], "1f.1"],
["What does the abolition of the average-premium system (doorsneesystematiek) under the Wtp mean?", [["Each participant gets an age-independent premium, so young people accrue relatively more than before", "Previously an equal accrual percentage applied for an equal premium; now the premium at each age produces its own accrual."], ["The premium rises as the participant gets older, so that older employees build up more pension", "A rising premium (scale) was precisely characteristic of old premium schemes; the Wtp assumes a flat premium."], ["Each participant accrues the same percentage of pension each year over their pension base, regardless of age", "That was precisely the average-premium system that is disappearing."], ["The AOW will from now on be paid by pension funds", "The AOW remains a national insurance scheme through the SVB (Dutch Social Insurance Bank)."]], "1h.13"],
["Why must social partners pay attention to compensation in the transition to the new system?", [["Because middle-aged and older employees in particular may be disadvantaged by the move to a flat premium", "In their younger years they accrued relatively little and, with a flat premium, accrue less later than under the average-premium system."], ["Because young people receive a lower AOW because of the Wtp", "The Wtp does not change the AOW."], ["Because after the transition employers no longer have to pay premiums and employees bear the full premium themselves", "Employers continue to pay premiums in the new system."], ["Because retirees have to repay their entire benefit", "Retirees do not have to repay anything."]], "1h.13"],
["What is meant by the transfer of accrued pension rights (invaren) in the transition?", [["Converting accrued pension entitlements and rights into the new contribution scheme", "After the transfer, old rights too are continued in the new contract as personal pension assets or a benefit."], ["An employee moving to another employer, with their pension going to the new provider", "That leads at most to value transfer, not to invaren."], ["Cashing in all pensions on the move", "Invaren precisely means that the rights remain in the new contract."], ["Registering new employees with a pension fund", "That is the enrolment of participants, not invaren."]], "1h.4"],
["What is the final date by which pension schemes must have moved to the new Wtp system?", [["1 January 2028", "The Wtp transition period runs until 1 January 2028 at the latest."], ["1 January 2027", "That was the original end date; it has been shifted to 1 January 2028."], ["1 July 2023", "The Wtp entered into force on 1 July 2023; that is the start, not the end of the transition."], ["31 December 2029", "The transition period does not run until the end of 2029."]], "1h.13"],
["On what date did the Pension Transition Act (Wtp) enter into force?", [["1 July 2023", "From that date the transition period to the new system ran."], ["1 January 2022", "In 2022 the bill was still before parliament."], ["1 January 2025", "On that date some funds made the switch, but the act applied earlier."], ["1 January 2028", "That is the final transition date, not the date of entry into force."]], "1h.13"],
["Jolanda (55) has worked in healthcare for thirty years and accrues pension at a large industry-wide pension fund. The fund has decided to transfer the accrued pensions into the new solidarity contribution scheme (invaren). Jolanda has a bad feeling about this and wants to keep her pension in the old scheme. She asks her adviser whether she can personally object to the transfer. What is correct?", [["No, there is no individual right of objection; the fund board must weigh the interests in a balanced way", "The Wtp provides no individual right of objection against invaren; the board must make a balanced weighing of interests, involving the fund's bodies."], ["Yes, every participant can submit an individual written objection within six months of the transition decision", "Such an individual right of objection against invaren is not in the Wtp."], ["Yes, but only participants aged 55 and over, because they are closest to retirement", "For older participants too there is no individual right of objection against invaren."], ["No, but she can demand that her pension be cashed in or transferred before the transition", "The transition gives no right to cash in or to an individual transfer to avoid invaren."]], "1h.13"],
["How is partner's pension before the retirement date arranged under the Wtp in principle?", [["On a risk basis, with a maximum level linked to salary", "As a result the cover no longer depends on the number of years of service; the law sets a maximum of 50% of salary."], ["On an accrual basis, depending on the number of years of service with the current employer", "The Wtp chooses the risk basis so that the level does not depend on length of service."], ["Partner's pension has been abolished under the Wtp", "Partner's pension remains, but on a risk basis."], ["As a fixed amount that is the same for every participant", "The level is related to salary, not a fixed amount."]], "1i.5"],
["Adviser Mirjam is preparing a new pension scheme at a bakery incorporated as a BV (private limited company). The manager wants to sign the pension agreement on behalf of the BV and says he 'always arranges that sort of thing'. Mirjam consults the Trade Register of the Chamber of Commerce. It shows that only the two directors together are authorised to represent the BV. What should Mirjam do?", [["Have it signed by the directors who are authorised according to the Trade Register, or by someone with their power of attorney", "Only someone who is authorised to represent the BV, or who has a power of attorney for it, can validly bind the BV."], ["Nothing; a manager is always authorised to sign pension agreements on behalf of the BV", "A manager is not automatically authorised to represent; that appears from the Trade Register or a power of attorney."], ["Have the signature confirmed by the works council, which can then represent the BV", "The works council has co-determination rights but does not represent the BV."], ["Have the agreement signed on behalf of the BV by the pension provider", "The provider is another party and cannot represent the BV."]], "1b.1"],
["What does the choice of a variable pension benefit in the new system mean?", [["The benefit can move with investment results and developments in life expectancy", "A variable benefit can rise and fall; shocks can, however, be spread over several years."], ["The benefit is guaranteed and rises annually with inflation", "A variable benefit is precisely not guaranteed."], ["The participant chooses each month the amount they draw", "A variable benefit too is a periodic pension benefit under fixed rules, not free withdrawal."], ["The benefit stops as soon as the personal pension assets run out, regardless of the retiree's age", "A pension benefit is in principle lifelong."]], "1f.5"],
["After the end of the transition, is a defined benefit agreement still a permitted form for new pension accrual?", [["No, new accrual then takes place in a new-style defined contribution agreement", "The Wtp ends new accrual in defined benefit agreements."], ["Yes, employers may freely choose between a defined benefit agreement and a defined contribution agreement", "After the transition, new accrual in a defined benefit agreement is no longer permitted."], ["Yes, but only for employees over 50", "There is no age exception for new accrual in a defined benefit agreement."], ["Yes, if the employer itself guarantees the benefit", "An employer guarantee does not make new accrual in a defined benefit agreement possible."]], "1h.13"],
["Ahmed (52) is an account manager at an ICT company. He has a contribution scheme with an age-dependent premium scale, so his premium rises every year. His employer is switching to a contribution scheme under the Pension Transition Act, in which new participants get a flat premium. Ahmed fears his premium will fall sharply. What may apply to him?", [["Employer and employees can opt for grandfathering (eerbiedigende werking), so that his scale continues under conditions", "The Wtp allows existing participants in a contribution scheme with a scale to keep that scale under conditions."], ["His scale must in all cases be reversed retroactively to a flat premium for everyone", "There is no retroactive effect, and grandfathering is precisely possible."], ["He must pay the difference between the old and the new premium himself to keep his accrual", "The law imposes no obligation on the employee to pay extra."], ["He loses the pension assets he has already built up in the old contribution scheme", "Accrued assets remain the participant's; the switch does not affect that."]], "1h.12"],
["How are expected pension benefits shown to participants in the new system?", [["In different scenarios, such as an expected, an optimistic and a pessimistic scenario", "In this way the participant sees that the pension is not fixed and can move with the economy."], ["As one guaranteed amount that is fixed at the start of the benefit and can no longer change", "In the new system the benefit is not guaranteed."], ["Exclusively as the total amount of all premiums paid", "Premiums paid alone say little about the expected benefit."], ["Only as a percentage of the last-earned salary", "A replacement ratio can help, but the statutory communication works with scenarios."]], "1g.13"],
["What information must participants at least receive from their pension provider around the transition?", [["Personal information about their pension before and after the switch, so that the effect is visible", "Participants must be able to see what the switch means for their own pension."], ["An offer to cash in the pension instead of switching", "The transition offers no cashing-in option as an alternative."], ["A request to choose a new pension provider themselves", "The choice of provider lies with the employer and social partners, not with the participant."], ["Exclusively general information about the act and the transition, without personal details of their own entitlements", "General information is not enough; personal information is precisely what matters."]], "1h.13"],
["Willemijn (59) has received a letter from her pension fund about the move to the new system. It says that she will soon have personal pension assets. At a birthday party she hears that she can later freely withdraw that 'pot of money'. She wants to use it to repay her mortgage on her retirement date. What is the adviser's correct response?", [["The assets remain intended for a pension benefit; on the retirement date she can, however, withdraw up to 10% as a lump sum", "In the new system too the assets are intended for a lifelong benefit; free withdrawal is not possible, a lump sum of up to 10% is."], ["That is right; from the retirement date she may freely withdraw all the assets if she pays box 1 tax on them", "Pension assets cannot be freely withdrawn; they must be converted into a benefit."], ["That is right; she can even request the assets before the retirement date to repay the mortgage", "Early withdrawal to repay a mortgage is not permitted."], ["On the switch the assets go to the AOW, which will therefore be higher", "The AOW is a separate national insurance scheme and receives no pension assets."]], "1g.5"],
["What is the Witteveen framework (Witteveenkader)?", [["The tax framework in the Wage Tax Act that determines the maximum tax-facilitated pension accrual or premium", "Within this framework the reverse-taxation rule (omkeerregel) applies; above it the accrual is not tax-facilitated."], ["DNB's financial assessment framework for the financial position of pension funds, with requirements for buffers and funding ratio", "DNB's financial assessment framework concerns buffers, not tax limits."], ["The rules for dividing pension on divorce", "The division of pension on divorce is set out in the Wvps."], ["The rules for AOW accrual by migrants", "AOW accrual is regulated in the General Old Age Pensions Act."]], "1g.8"],
["What does the reverse-taxation rule (omkeerregel) mean for pension?", [["Premiums and entitlements are untaxed or deductible during accrual; the benefits are taxed", "The levying of tax is deferred until the moment of payout."], ["Premiums are taxed and the benefits are untaxed", "That system applies to net pension and net annuity, not to the reverse-taxation rule."], ["Both premiums and benefits are untaxed", "Full exemption does not exist; the benefit is taxed."], ["The employer pays the tax on the benefit instead of the employee, as a final levy through the payroll tax return", "The retiree pays tax on the pension benefit themselves."]], "1g.10"],
["What happens for tax purposes if a pension scheme exceeds the limits of the Witteveen framework?", [["The scheme becomes excessive and loses its tax status, so that the entitlement may be taxed as wages", "An excessive scheme is non-compliant; this leads to taxation of the employee."], ["Only the excess part is taxed, and only on payout, without consequences for the rest of the pension scheme", "The consequence is more far-reaching: the scheme loses its status as a pension scheme."], ["The employer must pay the pension provider a fine", "There is no fine for the provider; the consequence is fiscal."], ["Nothing happens; the Witteveen framework is a guideline without consequences", "Exceeding the tax framework does have tax consequences."]], "1g.8"],
["What is the offset (franchise) in a pension scheme?", [["Part of the salary over which no pension accrues because the AOW already provides for it", "Pensionable salary minus the offset is the pension base."], ["The maximum pensionable salary above which no tax-facilitated accrual is possible any more", "That is the cap (the maximum pensionable salary), not the offset."], ["The excess (eigen risico) the participant pays in case of incapacity for work", "The offset has nothing to do with incapacity for work."], ["The part of the premium that the employee pays themselves", "That is the employee contribution."]], "1h.3"],
["What does the Wtp change in the approach of the Witteveen framework?", [["The tax limit is expressed as a maximum premium instead of a maximum accrual percentage", "For new-style contribution schemes a premium limit fits better than an accrual limit."], ["The tax framework lapses entirely; every premium is deductible", "A tax maximum continues to apply."], ["The reverse-taxation rule is replaced by taxation in box 3", "The reverse-taxation rule remains; pension does not fall in box 3."], ["Pension accrual is only tax-facilitated over the salary up to the offset, above it through net pension", "The offset is precisely the part over which no pension is accrued."]], "1g.8"],
["Until when may an old-age pension, for tax purposes, start at the latest?", [["At the latest five years after the AOW age", "Deferral of the pension is permitted for tax purposes up to five years after the AOW age."], ["At the latest on the AOW age; deferral is not permitted", "Deferral beyond the AOW age is possible, up to a maximum."], ["At the latest ten years after the AOW age", "Ten years is longer than is permitted for tax purposes."], ["There is no latest start date", "A latest start date does apply for tax purposes."]], "1g.5"],
["What is the maximum share of the value of the old-age pension that a participant can have paid out as a lump sum on the pension start date?", [["10%", "The participant may withdraw at most 10% of the value of their old-age pension as a lump sum on the start date."], ["25%", "25% is more than the law permits; the maximum is 10%."], ["7.5%", "The maximum is higher, namely 10%."], ["50%", "Withdrawing such a large share as a lump sum is not permitted; the maximum is 10%."]], "1g.5"],
["Joke (67) retires next month from the pension fund of the municipality where she worked. She is single, rents an apartment and receives rent benefit (huurtoeslag). The fund offers her the option of taking part of her pension as a lump sum. She wants to use it to buy a new car. What should the adviser in any case point out to her?", [["The lump sum is taxed in box 1, may affect her rent benefit and permanently reduces her monthly pension", "The lump sum counts as income in the year of withdrawal, which may affect benefits, and the lifelong pension becomes lower."], ["The lump sum is untaxed because tax has already been paid on the premium, and it does not affect her benefits", "Pension falls under the reverse-taxation rule: the withdrawal is taxed and counts towards the income used for the means test."], ["Her monthly pension stays the same; the lump sum comes on top and is taxed in box 3", "The lump sum comes at the expense of the periodic benefit and is taxed in box 1."], ["She can request the lump sum at any time after the retirement date, until her 75th birthday at the latest", "The choice of a lump sum must be made when the pension starts."]], "1g.5"],
["When is the premium for an annuity (lijfrente) deductible in box 1?", [["When there is a pension shortfall, within the annual margin (jaarruimte) or reservation margin (reserveringsruimte)", "Annuity premium is only deductible to the extent that the taxpayer has a pension shortfall."], ["Always in full, regardless of the pension already accrued through the employer", "The deduction is limited to the annual margin and reservation margin."], ["Only if the annuity is taken out with a pension fund", "An annuity can be held with an insurer or a bank; a pension fund is not required."], ["Only if the premium is paid by the employer", "An annuity is precisely an individual provision that the client pays themselves."]], "1g.10"],
["In risk management, what is meant by the risk appetite (risicoacceptatiegraad) of an organisation?", [["The amount of risk an organisation is willing to accept deliberately in order to achieve its objectives", "The risk appetite indicates how much and what kind of risk the organisation deliberately wants to run in pursuing its objectives."], ["The permitted deviation around a set risk standard", "That is risk tolerance: the margin around the chosen standard."], ["The total amount that an organisation has insured against risks", "An insured amount says nothing about how much risk the organisation is willing to run."], ["The total amount for which an organisation has insured itself against risks with insurers", "The number of risks identified is no measure of the willingness to run risk."]], "1c.6"],
["An employer agrees with their adviser that annual pension costs may deviate by at most 10% from the budgeted amount. Which risk management concept fits this agreement best?", [["Risk tolerance", "Risk tolerance is the acceptable deviation around an objective or standard, here 10% around the budget."], ["Risk awareness", "Risk awareness is about recognising risks, not about a permitted deviation."], ["Enterprise risk management", "Enterprise risk management is the broad approach to risks across the whole organisation, not a deviation margin."], ["Risk appetite", "Risk appetite is about how much risk the organisation is willing to run in general; the margin around a standard is the tolerance."]], "1c.7"],
["What is a tax consequence when a tax-facilitated annuity (lijfrente) is cashed in in one go?", [["The cash-in sum is taxed in box 1 and revision interest (revisierente) may be due", "Because the premium was deductible earlier, the cash-in is taxed and revision interest may be levied on the value."], ["The cash-in sum is untaxed because it concerns own savings that were already taxed in box 3", "The premium was deducted earlier; the cash-in sum is therefore taxed."], ["The cash-in sum falls in box 3 at the deemed return", "Cashing in a facilitated annuity is taxed in box 1."], ["Cashing in an annuity is never permitted by law", "Cashing in is possible, but has tax consequences."]], "1j.5"],
["When analysing an employer's annual accounts, the adviser looks at the current ratio. What does this ratio express?", [["The ratio between current assets and short-term debts", "The current ratio shows whether the company can meet its short-term debts with its current assets."], ["The ratio between equity and total capital", "That is a solvency ratio."], ["Net profit as a percentage of equity", "That is the return on equity."], ["The ratio between pension costs and the total wage bill", "That is not a standard liquidity ratio; the current ratio concerns assets and debts."]], "1d.2"],
["Ilse (43) is a medical specialist employed by a hospital and earns well above the cap. On salary above that cap she no longer accrues tax-facilitated pension. Her employer therefore offers a voluntary net pension scheme. Ilse is considering joining and asks how it works for tax purposes. What is a characteristic of net pension?", [["The contribution is not deductible and the later benefit is untaxed", "Net pension is paid from net salary and is exempt in box 3; the benefit is therefore untaxed."], ["The contribution is deductible and the later benefit is taxed in box 1", "That is the reverse-taxation rule for ordinary pension; net pension works the other way round."], ["The employer is obliged to pay the full premium for the net pension", "Participation is voluntary and is paid from the employee's net salary."], ["The accrued assets count each year as assets in box 3", "Net pension is precisely exempt in box 3."]], "1g.10"],
["Where can a private individual place a tax-facilitated annuity (lijfrente) in the accrual phase?", [["With an insurer, or with a bank or investment institution through an annuity account or annuity investment right", "Since the introduction of bank savings for retirement (banksparen), annuity can also be built up with a bank."], ["Exclusively with an industry-wide pension fund", "An industry-wide pension fund provides second-pillar pension, not individual annuities."], ["Exclusively with the SVB", "The SVB administers national insurance schemes and does not offer annuities."], ["In an ordinary savings account in their own name without blocking, provided the client does not withdraw the balance before their AOW age", "For tax facilitation the balance must be blocked and meet conditions."]], "1g.10"],
["Since when can a dga (director-major shareholder) no longer build up new pension in own management (pensioen in eigen beheer)?", [["Since 1 April 2017", "With the Act on the phasing out of pension in own management, further accrual ended on 1 April 2017."], ["Since 1 January 2015", "On that date tax-facilitated pension accrual was limited, but pension in own management still existed."], ["Since 1 January 2020", "On that date accrual had already ended years earlier."], ["Since 1 July 2023", "That is the Wtp's date of entry into force, not the date of the phasing out of pension in own management."]], "1j.3"],
["What options did a dga have when pension in own management was phased out?", [["Leaving it paid-up, cashing in with a tax discount or converting it into a retirement obligation (oudedagsverplichting)", "Cashing in with a discount was only possible temporarily; leaving it paid-up and the retirement obligation remained as options."], ["Transferring the pension to the SVB as a supplement to the AOW, or paying it out as dividend from the BV", "Pension in own management cannot be transferred to the SVB."], ["Continuing accrual in own management until the retirement date", "Further accrual has precisely ended."], ["Converting the pension into a net pension in own management", "A net pension too cannot be built up in own management."]], "1j.3"],
["What is a retirement obligation (oudedagsverplichting, ODV)?", [["An obligation of the BV to pay the dga periodically from a certain age, arising from pension in own management", "With the ODV the partner's pension lapses; the value remains in the BV."], ["A mandatory annuity that every dga must take out with an insurer on salary above the cap", "The ODV is an obligation of the dga's own BV, not an insurance."], ["The statutory obligation of every employer with staff to offer employees a supplementary pension from the AOW age", "A general employer obligation to provide pension does not exist."], ["An AOW supplement for entrepreneurs", "The ODV is separate from the AOW."]], "1j.3"],
["Gerrit (62) is the dga of a transport company and has built up pension in own management in his BV. He is married to Marjan, who is entitled to a partner's pension under that scheme. Gerrit wants to convert his pension in own management into a retirement obligation after all. Marjan does not know yet. What is needed for the conversion?", [["Marjan's written consent, because she loses her entitlement to partner's pension", "On conversion into an ODV the partner's pension lapses; the partner must therefore consent in writing."], ["Prior permission from the Tax and Customs Administration, to be requested through advance tax consultation", "Advance consultation with the Tax and Customs Administration is not required for this conversion."], ["A decision by the AFM, because it concerns a change to a pension product", "The AFM has no role in the conversion of pension in own management."], ["Nothing; Gerrit decides independently as dga without Marjan having to be involved", "Because Marjan loses her partner's pension, her consent is precisely required."]], "1j.16"],
["Why could a dga with a substantial interest (aanmerkelijk belang) previously build up pension in own management while ordinary employees were not allowed to?", [["Because the obligation to place pension (onderbrengingsplicht) of the Pensions Act does not apply to the director-major shareholder", "The Pensions Act protects employees; the obligation to place pension externally did not apply to the dga."], ["Because the dga receives no AOW", "The dga is simply entitled to AOW; that was not the reason."], ["Because the AFM issued a licence for it", "No AFM licence was needed for pension in own management."], ["Because the BV paid premiums for it to an industry-wide pension fund, which lent the pension back to the BV", "With pension in own management the pension precisely remained within the dga's own BV."]], "1j.19"],
["How can a dga still save with tax facilitation for their old age after the phasing out of pension in own management?", [["Through a pension scheme with an external provider, such as an insurer, or through an annuity (lijfrente) within the annual margin", "Accrual in own management is no longer possible, but external placement and annuity are."], ["By building up pension in own management again in a second, newly established BV of their own, separate from the operating company", "In another BV of their own, too, pension in own management can no longer be built up."], ["By having the AOW age brought forward for tax purposes", "The AOW age is set by law and cannot be brought forward for tax purposes."], ["By parking private assets tax-exempt in box 2", "Such an exemption does not exist."]], "1j.20"],
["What role does the dga's salary play in an external pension scheme?", [["The pension base is based on the salary actually received from the BV, within the tax limits", "The pension must fit the salary the dga actually receives; dividend does not count."], ["Dividend payments count in full as pensionable salary because the dga is also a shareholder of the BV", "Dividend is not salary and is not pensionable."], ["The dga may choose any pension base", "The base must align with the actual salary and the tax rules."], ["Salary plays no role because the dga is not an employee", "For tax purposes the dga is an employee of their BV and salary does play a role."]], "1j.20"],
["A dga has left their pension in own management paid-up. What does that mean?", [["The accrued entitlements remain in the BV, but no new accrual is added", "The BV continues to have the obligation to pay out the accrued pension."], ["The pension has thereby been transferred automatically to an insurer, which takes over further administration", "Leaving it paid-up precisely means that it stays in the BV."], ["The pension has been cashed in and taxed", "Cashing in is a different choice from leaving it paid-up."], ["The BV may simply drop the pension obligation", "The BV continues to have the obligation towards the dga and their partner."]], "1j.6"],
["What restriction applies to a premium pension institution (PPI)?", [["A PPI may only carry out contribution agreements and may not itself bear biometric risks such as death", "A PPI must reinsure death and incapacity risks or place them with an insurer."], ["A PPI may only carry out defined benefit agreements and must hold a solvency buffer for them", "A PPI is precisely intended for defined contribution agreements."], ["A PPI may only carry out pension schemes for government employers and institutions in the semi-public sector", "A PPI can be used by employers in all sectors."], ["A PPI may not invest the premiums", "Investing premiums is precisely the core of a PPI."]], "1h.23"],
["What is an industry-wide pension fund (bedrijfstakpensioenfonds)?", [["A pension fund for an entire industry, in which the minister can make participation mandatory", "After mandatory participation is declared, employers in that industry must join, unless an exemption applies."], ["A pension fund for a single company or group", "That is a company pension fund."], ["A fund for members of a liberal profession, such as medical specialists, notaries and pharmacists", "That is a professional group pension fund."], ["A fund run by an insurer under an insurance licence from DNB", "An industry-wide pension fund is an independent foundation, not an insurer."]], "1g.8"],
["What is a characteristic of a general pension fund (algemeen pensioenfonds, APF)?", [["It can carry out the schemes of several employers in financially separate collectivity circles", "Each circle has its own assets, so that shortfalls are not passed on to other circles."], ["It carries out the AOW exclusively", "The AOW is carried out by the SVB (Dutch Social Insurance Bank)."], ["It is an insurer that also offers banking services", "An APF is a pension fund, not an insurer or a bank."], ["It may only serve employers with fewer than 50 employees that are not subject to mandatory participation", "No limit based on the number of employees applies to an APF."]], "1g.11"],
["Which supervisors are involved with pension providers?", [["DNB supervises prudentially and the AFM supervises conduct, including pension communication", "DNB safeguards financial soundness, the AFM among other things the provision of information to participants."], ["Only the AFM, because pension is a financial product and it also safeguards financial soundness", "Financial soundness falls under DNB."], ["Only DNB, because pension funds have no clients", "The AFM also supervises, for example pension communication."], ["The SVB and the UWV (Employee Insurance Agency) together", "The SVB and UWV are implementing bodies, not supervisors of pension providers."]], "1a.4"],
["Stefan owns an architecture firm with 25 employees. His company does not fall under a mandatory industry-wide pension fund. He wants to introduce a contribution scheme with a partner's pension on a risk basis. He asks his adviser which kinds of providers he can approach for this. What is correct?", [["A pension insurer, a PPI with reinsurance of the death risk, or an APF that is open for this", "All these providers can carry out a contribution scheme; a PPI may not bear the death risk itself and has it reinsured."], ["Only a PPI, because insurers do not carry out contribution schemes and funds only mandatory schemes", "Insurers do carry out contribution schemes, and an APF is also open to voluntary participation."], ["Only a bank with an annuity licence, which reinsures the death risk", "A bank is not a pension provider within the meaning of the Pensions Act."], ["His own company, by carrying out the scheme in own management", "The obligation to place pension applies to employees; own management is not permitted."]], "1i.11"],
["What information must an adviser in any case gather for good pension advice to a private individual?", [["Financial position, knowledge and experience, objectives, risk appetite and existing AOW and pension entitlements", "Only with that complete picture of the client can the advice be suitable."], ["Only gross annual income and desired retirement age, because the rest appears from the national online pension overview", "Income is one component of the client profile, not the whole of it."], ["Only the desired retirement age", "The retirement age is a wish, not a complete client profile."], ["Only the UPO from the last employer and gross annual income, because the AOW is the same for everyone", "One UPO does not give a complete picture; the AOW, other pensions and the personal situation also count."]], "1h.14"],
["What does the duty of care of a pension provider involve in a contribution scheme with investment choices?", [["The provider must guide the participant in making choices and take their risk profile into account", "The participant bears investment risk; the provider must therefore help with suitable choices."], ["The provider guarantees a minimum benefit on the retirement date, at least equal to the sum of the premiums paid", "A duty of care is not a guarantee of a particular benefit."], ["The provider does not have to do anything; the participant is responsible themselves", "The law precisely imposes a duty of care on the provider."], ["The provider must place the participant's pension assets with a bank so that there is no investment risk any more", "That is not how the duty of care is fulfilled."]], "1f.1"],
["Thomas (66) has a contribution scheme with an insurer through his employer and will retire in a few months. On his retirement date a substantial capital sum is available. A friend told him that other insurers sometimes offer a higher benefit for the same capital. Thomas asks whether he may purchase his benefit elsewhere. What is correct?", [["Yes, he has the shop right (shoprecht) and can in principle buy a benefit elsewhere", "With a defined contribution agreement the participant may in principle use the capital to buy a benefit from another provider."], ["No, the benefit must always be purchased from his own provider at the rate in the regulations", "The shop right precisely gives the possibility of purchasing elsewhere."], ["Yes, but only at a bank, as a bank annuity that he can withdraw freely", "The capital must be converted into a pension benefit and cannot be withdrawn freely."], ["No, shopping around is only possible with a defined benefit agreement and not with a contribution scheme", "The shop right precisely belongs to the defined contribution agreement."]], "1g.13"],
["An employer asks an adviser to select a new collective pension scheme. What belongs to careful advice?", [["Inventorying the wishes and situation of employer and employees, comparing providers and costs, and recording the choice", "In this way the employer can make a well-founded choice that fits their objectives and budget."], ["Immediately choosing the provider with the lowest premium, because cover and service are regulated identically for all providers by law", "Premium alone is insufficient; cover, costs and quality of implementation also count."], ["Only having the employees vote on the provider and recording the result of the vote in the collective labour agreement (cao)", "The employer chooses; support among employees and any right of consent of the works council are, however, relevant."], ["Leaving the choice to the supervisor", "The supervisor does not advise employers on the choice of a provider."]], "1c.12"],
["Harm (67) is retiring soon and is married to Riet, who has a small AOW supplement. His pension fund offers him a choice of a high-low construction, exchange between old-age and partner's pension, and a lump sum. Harm also receives healthcare benefit (zorgtoeslag). He asks his adviser which choice is best. What is the correct approach?", [["Look at the choices in conjunction with the financial situation, Riet, benefits and taxation, and explain the consequences", "Pension choices influence each other and have consequences for the partner, tax and benefits; good advice weighs these together."], ["Always advise the maximum lump sum, because then Harm can dispose of his pension assets himself", "A lump sum reduces the lifelong pension and may affect benefits; it is not always wise."], ["Only advise the choice with the highest gross amount, because that also always yields the most net", "A higher gross amount does not always yield more net because of tax and benefits."], ["Leave the choices to the pension provider, because it knows the scheme best", "The provider guides on choices but does not advise Harm on his overall situation."]], "1g.5"],
["What is Pension 1-2-3 (Pensioen 1-2-3)?", [["Layered pension information: layer 1 the essentials, layer 2 more depth and layer 3 all details and documents", "In this way participants can decide for themselves how deeply they delve into the information."], ["A step-by-step plan for applying for the AOW", "The AOW application runs through the SVB and has nothing to do with Pension 1-2-3."], ["Three mandatory choices a participant must make each year: retirement age, investment profile and partner cover", "Pension 1-2-3 is an information format, not a moment of choice."], ["A classification of pension funds by risk", "It is not a risk classification of providers."]], "1g.13"],
["What can a participant find in the national online pension overview that they can view with their DigiD?", [["An overview of the AOW and the pension accrued through employers at the various providers", "By logging in with DigiD the user sees their first- and second-pillar entitlements together."], ["A complete overview of all bank accounts and savings", "Ordinary bank balances are not on the national online pension overview."], ["A guaranteed calculation of net disposable income after retirement, including benefits and tax", "The overview shows gross entitlements and indications, not a guarantee of net income."], ["A comparison of pension providers with a ranking", "The site does not compare providers."]], "1h.14"],
["A client prints their national online pension overview for pension advice. What else should the adviser generally ask about?", [["Their own third-pillar provisions, such as annuities and bank savings for retirement, and the partner's situation", "This information is generally not on the overview, but is needed for complete advice."], ["Nothing; the overview contains all relevant pension information", "Third-pillar products and the partner's situation are usually missing."], ["Only the AOW details, because they are not on the overview", "The AOW is precisely on the overview."], ["Only the pensions from abroad, because the third pillar and partner details are already on it", "Annuities and partner details are precisely not on the overview; foreign pensions are also generally missing."]], "1h.14"],
["What is an important objective of the Pension Communication Act (Wet pensioencommunicatie)?", [["To make participants better understand what their pension involves, with information that matches their needs", "With layered information and digital possibilities, pension is to become more comprehensible."], ["To make pension advice mandatory for every employee before they make a choice in their pension scheme", "The law does not oblige anyone to seek advice."], ["To abolish the Uniform Pension Overview", "The UPO still exists."], ["To transfer all pension communication to the AFM", "The provider remains responsible for communication; the AFM supervises."]], "1h.13"],
["What must an insurance distributor under the IDD in any case establish before concluding an insurance contract?", [["The client's wishes and needs, so that the product offered fits them", "This obligation also applies when no advice is given."], ["The client's credit registration number", "A check in the credit registration belongs to credit and not to the IDD obligation."], ["The client's pension assets with the employer, as stated on the most recent UPO", "That may be relevant, but is not the general IDD obligation."], ["Whether the client has previously cancelled an insurance policy", "The IDD asks for wishes and needs, not the cancellation history."]], "2c.1"],
["What is an advantage of asset pooling within a general pension fund (APF)?", [["Circles can invest jointly, which can give economies of scale and lower costs", "With asset pooling the assets of circles are invested jointly, while each circle remains financially separate."], ["Shortfalls in one circle are automatically topped up from the assets of another circle", "Collectivity circles are financially separate; a shortfall is not paid from another circle."], ["Through joint investing the APF does not need a licence from DNB", "An APF always needs a licence from DNB."], ["Investment risk disappears entirely for the participants", "Joint investing changes nothing about the existence of investment risk."]], "1f.4"],
["At an employer the pension scheme is fully regulated in substance in the collective labour agreement (cao) that applies to it. Does the works council have a right of consent on the introduction of that scheme?", [["No, to the extent that the cao already regulates the scheme in substance, the right of consent lapses", "The works council's right of consent does not apply to the extent that a subject is already regulated in substance in a cao."], ["Yes, the works council always has a right of consent on pension, even if the cao regulates everything", "The right of consent precisely lapses to the extent that the cao already regulates the matter in substance."], ["Yes, and the works council may then deviate from the cao to the detriment of the employees", "The works council cannot set aside a cao."], ["No, because the works council never has any power on pension", "Without a cao regulation the works council does have a right of consent on pension."]], "1g.9"],
["What must an institution do with an unusual transaction under the Wwft?", [["Report it without delay to FIU-Nederland (Financial Intelligence Unit)", "The report must be made without delay as soon as the unusual nature is known."], ["Report it to the AFM within thirty days", "Unusual transactions are reported to FIU-Nederland, not to the AFM."], ["Tell the client immediately that a report is being made", "It is precisely prohibited to inform the client of the report."], ["Report it only if the amount exceeds a fixed threshold", "Subjective indicators too can lead to a reporting obligation, regardless of the amount."]], "4a.1"],
["How are the tax rules for occupational pension and for annuities (lijfrente) mainly divided between the Wage Tax Act (Wet LB) and the Income Tax Act (Wet IB)?", [["The tax rules for occupational pension are in the Wet LB, those for annuities in the Wet IB", "For tax purposes the pension scheme falls in the wage sphere; the annuity is a provision in income tax."], ["Both occupational pension and annuities are regulated entirely in the Wet IB", "The tax framework for occupational pension is in the Wet LB."], ["Occupational pension falls under the Wet IB and annuities under the Wet LB", "It is exactly the other way round."], ["Both fall only under the Pensions Act; the tax acts play no role", "The Pensions Act regulates civil law and supervisory matters; the tax rules are in the tax acts."]], "1g.10"],
["A client who holds a politically prominent position wants to make a substantial annuity contribution. What does the Wwft require of the institution?", [["Enhanced customer due diligence, including into the source of the assets", "A politically exposed person carries a higher risk of, for example, corruption."], ["Nothing special; ordinary customer due diligence always suffices", "For a PEP (politically exposed person) enhanced customer due diligence is mandatory."], ["Refuse the business relationship immediately", "A PEP may be a client, but under enhanced measures."], ["A report to FIU-Nederland, regardless of the size or nature of the transaction", "PEP status is not in itself a reason for a report."]], "4a.1"],
["Which pillar does a mandatory professional pension scheme, for example for general practitioners or medical specialists, belong to?", [["The second pillar", "Collective schemes through the employer or the occupational group, including mandatory professional pension schemes, form the second pillar."], ["The third pillar", "The third pillar consists of individual, voluntary provision; a mandatory professional scheme is arranged collectively."], ["The first pillar", "The first pillar is the AOW, a government national insurance scheme for all residents, not a professional scheme."], ["None of the pillars, because they are self-employed", "Self-employed professionals too can accrue second-pillar pension through a mandatory professional pension scheme."]], "1g.8"],
["How is occupational pension in the second pillar mainly financed?", [["Through funding: premiums are invested and the pension is paid from them", "In the second pillar assets are built up and invested; the benefits are paid from that saved capital and the returns on it."], ["Through a pay-as-you-go system in which today's workers pay the current pensions of retirees", "A pay-as-you-go system is characteristic of the AOW in the first pillar, not of occupational pension."], ["Entirely from the general resources of the central government budget", "The government does not finance occupational pension; it is paid from employer and employee premiums and from investment returns."], ["Exclusively from the employer's premiums, without investment", "Premiums are precisely invested, and the employee too often contributes through their own contribution."]], "1f.3"],
["Pension planning often uses a target income. Which starting point is widely used in practice as a rule of thumb?", [["About 70% of the last-earned or average gross salary, including AOW", "A target income of around 70% of gross salary, AOW included, is a widely used rule of thumb; actual needs differ per client."], ["Exactly 100% of the last net salary, legally guaranteed", "There is no legal guarantee of a particular pension income; 100% net is not a common standard."], ["The net minimum wage, because the AOW is based on it", "The AOW is linked to the minimum wage, but an employee's target income is generally higher."], ["50% of gross salary, excluding AOW, as a statutory minimum standard", "The law prescribes no minimum level of supplementary pension; this is not a statutory standard."]], "1h.14"],
["What is an important risk of the third pillar compared with the second pillar?", [["Accrual depends on one's own discipline; there is no employer who contributes or shares risks collectively", "Individual provisions are only built up if the client contributes themselves, without an employer contribution or collective risk sharing."], ["Third-pillar products are never tax-facilitated", "Annuities and bank savings for retirement are tax-facilitated within the annual margin and reservation margin."], ["The benefit from the third pillar is always reduced against the AOW, because the AOW takes other income into account", "The AOW has no income or asset test, so third-pillar income does not lead to a reduction of the AOW."], ["A third-pillar provision lapses when changing employers", "An individual provision is independent of the employer and simply remains when changing jobs."]], "1c.5"],
["Linda (40) works as a self-employed person without staff (zzp'er) and has never accrued pension with an employer. Which pillars are expected to contribute to her retirement income if she arranges nothing extra?", [["Only the first pillar, the AOW", "Without occupational pension and own provisions Linda is entitled only to the AOW, provided she lives or works in the Netherlands."], ["The first and the second pillar", "Without an employment relationship or mandatory professional scheme a zzp'er does not accrue second-pillar pension."], ["The first and the third pillar", "The third pillar only arises if Linda makes a provision herself, such as an annuity."], ["No pillar at all, because she is an entrepreneur", "Entrepreneurs too are insured for the AOW as long as they live or work in the Netherlands."]], "1h.14"],
["Can someone bring forward or postpone the start date of their AOW at their own choice?", [["No, the AOW starts at the statutory AOW age and cannot be brought forward or postponed", "The AOW age is laid down by law; stopping work earlier must be bridged with own or pension funds."], ["Yes, it can be brought forward by up to five years before the AOW age, with a permanently lower benefit", "A flexible AOW with early start does not exist; that is possible with the old-age pension of the second pillar."], ["Yes, it can be postponed and then yields a higher AOW", "A postponement option with an increase does not exist for the AOW; that is a choice for supplementary pension."], ["Only bringing forward, and only in a heavy occupation", "Even for heavy occupations there is no early AOW; other arrangements exist for that through the employer."]], "1h.3"],
["An employer has a defined benefit agreement with a pension insurer, in which the purchase of the annual accrual per participant depends on age. The workforce will age in the coming years. What is the expected effect on pension costs?", [["The costs rise, because purchasing the same accrual is more expensive the older the participant is", "For an older participant there is less time for returns, so the same accrual costs more."], ["The costs fall, because older employees pay premiums for a shorter time", "The annual purchase precisely becomes more expensive the older the participant is."], ["The costs stay the same, because age plays no role in a defined benefit agreement", "With age-dependent purchase, age precisely plays a major role."], ["There is no effect, because only the insurer's funding ratio determines the costs", "An insurer does not have a funding ratio like a fund; the costs follow from the purchase rates."]], "1h.5"],
["An employer wants to exclude employees with a temporary contract from the pension scheme that applies to employees with a permanent contract. Is that permitted?", [["No, distinction between temporary and permanent contracts is prohibited, unless objectively justified", "The prohibition of distinction based on the duration of the employment contract also applies to pension."], ["Yes, temporary employees may always be excluded from the pension scheme", "Exclusion solely because of a temporary contract is contrary to the prohibition of distinction."], ["Yes, as long as the temporary contract lasts less than two years", "The law contains no such exemption for short contracts."], ["Only if the employer falls under a mandatory industry-wide pension fund", "Mandatory participation does not make it possible to exclude temporary employees."]], "1h.8"],
["Why is the tax rate in the first bracket lower for someone who has reached the AOW age than for someone younger?", [["Because an AOW recipient no longer pays AOW premium", "The national insurance premium for the AOW is part of the combined rate in the first bracket; after the AOW age that premium lapses."], ["Because pension income has its own, lower rate in box 2", "Pension income falls in box 1, not in box 2; box 2 concerns income from a substantial interest."], ["Because AOW recipients no longer owe Anw premium", "AOW recipients also still pay Anw and Wlz (Long-term Care Act) premium; the difference is due to the lapse of the AOW premium."], ["Because the general tax credit doubles after the AOW age", "Tax credits are precisely lower for AOW recipients; the lower rate is due to the lapse of the AOW premium."]], "1g.10"],
["Gerard is 66 and will reach the AOW age in a few months. He is married to Anja (59), who has had no income of her own for years. An acquaintance who retired in 2012 received a supplement at the time for his younger wife. Gerard also wants to apply for that supplement. Can he get a partner supplement (partnertoeslag) for Anja?", [["No, for new cases the partner supplement no longer exists; he receives AOW for people living together", "The partner supplement has been abolished for new cases; Gerard receives the AOW for married and cohabiting persons."], ["Yes, he receives a supplement on his AOW until Anja herself reaches the AOW age", "That arrangement no longer applies to anyone reaching the AOW age now."], ["Yes, because Anja has no income of her own, the partner supplement is then awarded on an income-dependent basis", "Even without income of the partner there is no partner supplement for new cases."], ["No, but Gerard receives instead the AOW for single persons as long as Anja is younger", "Married persons receive the AOW for people living together, regardless of the partner's age."]], "1h.3"],
["Are unmarried cohabiting AOW recipients treated as single for the AOW?", [["No, with a joint household they count as cohabiting, even without marriage", "The AOW looks at the actual living situation: anyone who runs a joint household with another receives the AOW for people living together."], ["Yes, only married persons and registered partners count as living together", "The AOW does not rely on civil status alone; unmarried cohabitants too can count as living together."], ["Yes, as long as they have no cohabitation agreement", "A cohabitation agreement is not decisive; what matters is actually running a joint household."], ["No, but only if they have lived together for more than ten years", "A minimum period of cohabitation is not a condition; running a joint household is decisive."]], "1h.3"],
["Rob is 70, single and receives AOW. His brother Frans has become seriously ill and can no longer live alone. Frans moves in with Rob so that Rob can care for him. Rob fears he will now be seen as living together and receive less AOW. What may apply to the level of Rob's AOW?", [["Under conditions an exception for informal care (mantelzorg) applies, so that Rob can keep the AOW for single persons", "Where care is provided within one home, an exception can apply under conditions, so that both continue to count as single."], ["Rob automatically receives an extra supplement on his AOW for the informal care he provides", "The AOW has no informal care supplement."], ["Rob's AOW stops entirely as long as his brother lives with him", "There is no ground on which the AOW stops because of someone living in."], ["Rob must have his AOW converted into social assistance because there is now a joint household", "The AOW continues; the only question is whether he counts as single or as living together."]], "1h.3"],
["Nina (35) is a software engineer who has always lived and worked in the Netherlands. She is offered a job in Toronto and emigrates to Canada next month. There she will work as an employee for a Canadian employer. Nina asks what happens to her AOW accrual. What is correct?", [["Her accrual stops in principle; under conditions she can insure herself voluntarily with the SVB", "You accrue AOW by living or working in the Netherlands; anyone who leaves can insure themselves voluntarily under conditions."], ["Her AOW accrual simply continues as long as she has Dutch nationality", "Accrual depends on living or working in the Netherlands, not on nationality."], ["She also loses the AOW she has accrued up to her departure", "The AOW already accrued is retained and will also be paid out abroad later."], ["Her AOW accrual is automatically continued through her Dutch pension fund", "A pension fund does not carry out the AOW; the SVB does."]], "1h.14"],
["When is there prohibited age discrimination in a pension scheme?", [["Distinction by age without objective justification and without a statutory exception", "Distinction by age is only permitted if it is objectively justified or falls under a statutory exception."], ["Always when the premium or accrual differs with age, even within a statutory exception to that", "The law precisely contains exceptions within which age distinction in pension is permitted."], ["Only if employees above the AOW age are excluded from participation", "Age discrimination can also arise at other ages and with other rules."], ["Never, because pension schemes fall outside the rules on equal treatment", "The rules on equal treatment also apply to pension."]], "1h.12"],
["Femke is 63 and works as a secondary school teacher. She wants to stop working and have her old-age pension start now. Her AOW age is still well over three years away. She fears her income in those first years will be too low. Which pension choice can help cover that temporary income gap?", [["A high-low construction: the pension pays out higher first, lower later", "With a high-low construction she receives a higher pension until her AOW age, which partly offsets the absence of the AOW."], ["Bringing forward her AOW so that it starts at the same time as her pension", "The AOW cannot be brought forward."], ["Taking out an Anw gap insurance that pays out until her AOW age", "An Anw gap insurance pays out on death, not on early retirement."], ["Applying for an Anw benefit that tops up the missing income until the AOW age", "The Anw is a survivor's benefit and does not apply on stopping work earlier."]], "1g.5"],
["What happens to the AOW of someone who keeps working as an employee after the AOW age?", [["The AOW is paid in full, regardless of earned income", "The AOW has no income test; continuing to work has no influence on its level, but does on the total tax burden."], ["The AOW is reduced by the salary earned", "A reduction for earned income applies to the Anw, not to the AOW."], ["The AOW is suspended until the employee stops", "The AOW starts at the AOW age and is not suspended by continuing to work."], ["The employee pays AOW premium again and accrues extra AOW", "After the AOW age no AOW premium is owed and no further accrual takes place."]], "1h.3"],
["A graphic design company switches its pension scheme from insurer A to insurer B on 1 January. Employee Ellen (51) has been ill since October of the previous year. After the waiting period she is declared incapacitated for work, so her right to premium waiver only starts after the switch. Her employer asks which insurer must provide for this. Which insurer in principle bears the premium waiver for Ellen?", [["Insurer A, because Ellen fell ill when the scheme was running there (run-off risk, uitlooprisico)", "Under the run-off covenant, the provider with which the participant was insured on the first day of illness bears the run-off risk."], ["Insurer B, because the incapacity for work was only established after the switch", "For cover, the first day of illness counts, not the moment of establishment."], ["Neither; the employer must continue paying the pension premium for Ellen itself", "The run-off arrangements precisely prevent Ellen from falling between two insurers."], ["The UWV (Employee Insurance Agency), which takes over the premium waiver when the insurer changes", "The UWV does not take over premium waiver when an insurer is changed."]], "1h.21"],
["Is an Anw survivor's benefit reduced if the surviving dependant also receives a partner's pension from the second pillar?", [["No, partner's pension does not count in the Anw income test", "The Anw looks at income from work and at benefits that replace it; a survivor's pension is not reduced."], ["Yes, the partner's pension is deducted in full from the Anw", "That is not so: the Anw income test concerns earned income and replacement benefits, not pension."], ["Yes, for half of the gross partner's pension", "There is no partial reduction for pension income; pension stays outside the test."], ["Only if the partner's pension is higher than the minimum wage", "No threshold applies for pension; pension income plays no role in the Anw income test."]], "1h.16"],
["What kind of income can lead to a reduction of an Anw survivor's benefit?", [["Income from work and benefits that replace it, such as WW (unemployment benefit) or the Sickness Benefits Act (Ziektewet)", "The Anw is a safety net with an income test on earned income and replacement benefits, with part of it disregarded."], ["A payout from a term life insurance", "A one-off payout from one's own insurance does not count as income for the Anw."], ["Assets in box 3, such as savings, investments and a second home above the tax-free allowance", "The Anw has no asset test; only certain income is taken into account."], ["The old-age pension of the deceased partner", "That pension ends on death; it is not income of the surviving dependant that affects the Anw."]], "1h.16"],
["Who can claim an Anw orphan's benefit?", [["A child both of whose parents have died, up to a legally determined age", "The Anw orphan's benefit is intended for full orphans; if one parent is still alive, there is no orphan's benefit from the Anw."], ["Any child one of whose parents has died", "For half-orphans the surviving parent may receive a survivor's benefit; there is no orphan's benefit for the child itself."], ["Only children of a deceased employee with a pension scheme", "That describes an orphan's pension from the second pillar, not the Anw as a national insurance scheme."], ["Adult children too, regardless of their age", "The orphan's benefit is tied to a maximum age and is not lifelong."]], "1i.5"],
["Esra (42) has been a widow since her husband died three years ago. She has a son of 16 and therefore receives an Anw survivor's benefit. Esra works part time and is not incapacitated for work. In two years her son turns 18. What then happens to her Anw benefit if there is no other ground for the Anw?", [["The Anw survivor's benefit ends", "If the care of a child under 18 was the only ground, the benefit ends when the child turns 18."], ["The benefit continues until her AOW age", "Without a valid entry ground, the Anw does not continue until the AOW age."], ["The benefit is converted into an orphan's benefit for her son", "An orphan's benefit is for children both of whose parents have died."], ["The benefit is halved, but then continues for life", "The Anw has no lifelong half benefit."]], "1h.16"],
["Bram has a pub and on 1 March hired Lisa (29) as manager. A pension scheme with an insurer is in place, with a partner's pension on a risk basis. Bram forgot to enrol Lisa. In June Lisa dies in a traffic accident. Her partner now asks about the partner's pension. What is the risk for Bram?", [["Bram may be liable for the partner's pension that would have been paid without his omission", "An employer who does not enrol an employee in time runs the risk of having to make good the missed cover himself."], ["None; the insurer must always pay the full partner's pension even without enrolment", "Whether there is cover without enrolment depends on the contract terms; there is no certainty."], ["None, because the Anw then fully takes over the missing partner's pension for the partner", "The Anw is a national insurance scheme with its own conditions and does not replace a missed partner's pension."], ["The insurer recovers the omission from Lisa's partner", "The partner did not cause the omission; the risk lies with the employer."]], "1h.21"],
["Dennis (50) is married to Mieke (48). They have no children. After a serious illness Mieke has been declared 50% incapacitated for work by the UWV (Employee Insurance Agency). Dennis asks his adviser whether Mieke could receive an Anw benefit if he dies. What is correct?", [["She may be entitled, because at least 45% incapacity for work is an entry ground", "A surviving dependant who is at least 45% incapacitated for work may be entitled; the income test can, however, reduce the benefit."], ["No, without a child under 18 there is never entitlement to an Anw benefit", "Incapacity for work of at least 45% is a separate entry ground."], ["Yes, she then always receives a full Anw benefit, without an income test", "Income from work or a replacement benefit can reduce the Anw."], ["Only if she has been declared fully and permanently incapacitated for work under the WIA", "The threshold is 45% incapacity for work, not full and permanent incapacity."]], "1h.16"],
["What role does a term life insurance (overlijdensrisicoverzekering) play in covering survivor risks alongside pension and the Anw?", [["On death it pays out a capital sum to cover loss of income or housing costs", "A term life insurance gives a one-off payout and is a flexible supplement to partner's pension and the Anw."], ["It permanently increases the surviving dependant's AOW", "The AOW is a national insurance scheme and is not increased by a private insurance."], ["It replaces the partner's pension that the employer is obliged to offer under the Pensions Act", "Employers are not obliged to offer partner's pension; a term life insurance is separate from the pension scheme."], ["It only pays out at the surviving dependant's AOW age", "A term life insurance pays out on death within the term, not at a fixed age."]], "1i.8"],
["May a pension provider require a medical examination before an employee can participate in their employer's pension scheme?", [["No, the Pensions Act prohibits a medical examination as a condition for participation", "Participation may not depend on health; this prevents employees in poor health from falling outside the scheme."], ["Yes, for partner's pension on a risk basis this is customary", "No medical selection may take place for the risk component of the collective scheme either."], ["Yes, if the employee is older than 50", "There is no age limit above which a medical examination is permitted for participation."], ["Only with a pension insurer, not with a pension fund", "The prohibition applies to all pension providers that carry out a pension agreement."]], "1i.3"],
["The metal company of Bart Kok (58) has an average-salary scheme with an insurer. Pension costs have risen sharply in recent years. Bart wants to unilaterally scale the scheme back to a contribution scheme. The pension agreement contains an amendment clause (wijzigingsbeding). When may he invoke that clause?", [["Only in the case of an interest so compelling that the employees' interest must reasonably yield", "A unilateral amendment through the amendment clause is only possible in the case of such a compelling interest of the employer."], ["Always, because the employer pays the premium and therefore decides on the content", "Paying the premium gives the employer no unlimited right to amend unilaterally."], ["Only if the employees do not object within a month after written notice", "Silence on the part of employees is not a statutory standard for a unilateral amendment."], ["Never; a pension scheme cannot be amended once introduced, even with an amendment clause", "With an amendment clause amendment is possible, but only in the case of a compelling interest."]], "1g.3"],
["May a participant pledge their pension entitlement to a bank as security for a loan?", [["No, pension entitlements cannot in principle be alienated, pledged or encumbered", "The prohibition on alienation protects the pension purpose, so that the pension remains available for old age and surviving dependants."], ["Yes, if the bank has a licence from DNB and the pledge has been reported to the provider", "A bank's licence does not change the statutory prohibition on pledging pension."], ["Yes, provided the partner gives written consent", "Partner consent is needed for, for example, exchange, but does not make pledging pension possible."], ["Only to finance an owner-occupied home", "The prohibition applies to an owner-occupied home too; pension cannot serve as collateral."]], "1j.5"],
["What does the prohibition on cashing in pension (afkoopverbod) in the Pensions Act mainly involve?", [["Cashing in is prohibited, except in statutory exceptions such as a small pension", "Cashing in would undermine the pension purpose; cashing in is therefore permitted only in limited exceptions."], ["Pension may always be cashed in if the participant wishes", "There is no free cash-in option; that would defeat the purpose of a lifelong provision."], ["Cashing in is only prohibited if the partner objects", "The prohibition on cashing in applies regardless of the partner's wishes; it is a statutory restriction."], ["Cashing in is fully permitted as soon as the participant has reached the AOW age and wishes it", "Reaching the AOW age gives no general right to cash in; the limited option of a lump sum does exist."]], "1j.5"],
["An employer applies a different premium for men than for women in its pension scheme. Is that permitted?", [["No, distinction by sex in pension schemes is not permitted", "Equal treatment of men and women also applies to pension; premiums and benefits must be gender-neutral."], ["Yes, because women live longer on average", "A difference in life expectancy does not justify distinction; the scheme must guarantee equal treatment."], ["Yes, if the distinction is included in the collective labour agreement (cao)", "A cao cannot set aside statutory rules on equal treatment."], ["Only with a defined contribution agreement, not with a defined benefit agreement", "The prohibition of distinction by sex applies to all types of pension agreements."]], "1h.11"],
["Joyce (36) works three days a week as an administrative employee at a wholesaler. Her full-time colleagues participate in the employer's pension scheme. When she joined she heard that part-timers are excluded from it. No particular reason was given for this exclusion. What is correct?", [["That is contrary to the prohibition of distinction based on working hours, unless objectively justified", "Employers may not exclude part-timers from a pension scheme without objective justification."], ["That is allowed, because the employer is free to choose who participates in the scheme", "The employer is bound by the prohibition of distinction based on working hours."], ["That is allowed, as long as Joyce works less than half the normal working hours", "No such limit exists; small part-time jobs are protected too."], ["That is allowed if the pension premium for part-timers would otherwise become too expensive", "Higher costs alone are generally not an objective justification."]], "1h.7"],
["Who must inform a new participant of the main features of the pension scheme after participation starts?", [["The pension provider, through a start letter or comparable information", "The Pensions Act places the duty to inform at the start of participation on the provider, who explains the essentials of the scheme."], ["The employee themselves, by requesting the pension regulations from the HR department", "The law precisely places the duty to inform on the provider; the participant does not have to ask for it."], ["The AFM, through a personal letter", "The AFM supervises communication, but does not itself inform participants about their scheme."], ["The UWV (Employee Insurance Agency), when registering the employment", "The UWV carries out employee insurance schemes and has no role in information about the pension scheme."]], "1h.16"],
["An employer does not offer a pension scheme. What must they do under the Pensions Act?", [["Inform the employee that they have no pension scheme", "In this way the employee knows they must arrange supplementary pension themselves; the employer has a duty to inform."], ["Take out a replacement annuity (lijfrente) for the employee", "The law does not oblige the employer to arrange an annuity if they offer no pension."], ["Pay a higher gross allowance as compensation", "There is no statutory duty to compensate; the employee must, however, be informed."], ["Nothing; in that case there is no obligation at all", "Even without a pension scheme the employer has a duty to inform the employee."]], "1h.16"],
["The construction company where Ferry (44) works as a carpenter is in financial difficulties. For several months it has not paid the premium to the industry-wide pension fund. The arrears have meanwhile grown considerably. Ferry and his colleagues know nothing about it. What must the pension fund do in the case of premium arrears of some size?", [["Inform the participants and the works council or employee representation", "In the case of premium arrears of some size the provider must inform the participants and the employee participation body."], ["Immediately stop the participants' pension accrual until the arrears are made up", "The pension entitlements remain; the fund can collect the premium from the employer."], ["Recover the arrears from the employees by withholding from their wages", "The employer is the premium debtor; the fund cannot recover the debt from the employees."], ["Immediately refer the matter to Kifid (Dutch Financial Services Complaints Institute) for binding advice", "Kifid is not a collection or supervisory body for premium arrears."]], "1i.1"],
["Marco (39) works as a welder at a machine factory. His employer goes bankrupt and the bankruptcy trustee dismisses all employees. It later turns out that the employer did not pay the pension premium for the last months to the insurer. Marco fears his accrued pension will now disappear. What can he expect?", [["The UWV (Employee Insurance Agency) can take over the outstanding pension premium for a limited period", "In a bankruptcy the UWV can pay outstanding premium for a limited period, so that accrual over that period is restored."], ["His accrued pension falls into the bankruptcy estate and is divided among the creditors", "The pension entitlements are placed with the provider and do not fall into the estate."], ["The insurer lets all accrued entitlements lapse because premium is missing", "The pension already accrued remains in place."], ["The bankruptcy trustee may cash in Marco's accrued pension for the benefit of the creditors", "The trustee has no say over pension placed with the provider."]], "1h.19"],
["The printing works of director Sandra (49) has 80 employees and a works council. No collective labour agreement (cao) applies. Sandra wants to introduce a new pension scheme with an insurer. The adviser is preparing the proposal. What right does the works council have on the introduction?", [["Right of consent", "If pension is not regulated in a cao, the works council has a right of consent on the introduction, amendment or withdrawal of a pension scheme."], ["Only a right to information afterwards", "The WOR (Works Councils Act) gives the works council more than just information afterwards on pension schemes."], ["A right of veto on the choice of each individual investment fund", "The right of consent concerns the scheme, not each individual investment fund."], ["No right at all; pension is a matter for the provider", "It is precisely in the pension scheme itself that the works council has an important role."]], "1g.6"],
["According to what principle must a pension fund invest its assets?", [["The prudent-person rule: carefully and in the interest of participants and retirees", "The Pensions Act requires the fund to invest as a prudent person would, with attention to risk and diversification."], ["Exclusively in Dutch government bonds", "The law prescribes no specific investment category; what matters is careful, diversified investment."], ["So as to achieve the highest possible return, regardless of the risks to participants", "Risk must fit the obligations; maximum return without regard to risk is not prudent."], ["According to the employer's investment wishes", "The fund board invests in the interest of all stakeholders, not according to the employer's wishes."]], "1f.3"],
["What does the funding ratio (dekkingsgraad) of a pension fund express?", [["The ratio of the fund's assets to the value of pension liabilities", "A funding ratio of 100% means that the assets are exactly equal to the value of the pensions promised."], ["The percentage of participants who have a partner's pension", "The funding ratio is a financial measure, not a measure of cover for survivor risks."], ["The ratio between premium income and the benefits the fund pays in a year", "That cash flow ratio says little about the financial position; the funding ratio compares assets with liabilities."], ["The part of the salary over which pension is accrued", "That is the pension base after deduction of the offset, not a concept for the fund's financial position."]], "1h.3"],
["What does conditional indexation (voorwaardelijke toeslagverlening) mean in a defined benefit scheme at a pension fund?", [["The fund increases pensions only if its financial position allows; there is no entitlement to it", "With conditional indexation the increase depends on fund policy and the funding ratio, and this must be clearly communicated."], ["The pension rises every year guaranteed in line with price inflation, as measured by Statistics Netherlands (CBS)", "A guaranteed increase is unconditional indexation; it is expensive and must be fully funded."], ["The pension is only increased if the participant pays extra", "Indexation is paid from the fund's return or a reserve intended for it, not from a contribution by the participant."], ["The employer is obliged to pay in a shortfall for indexation", "With conditional indexation there is no obligation on the employer to make additional payments."]], "1h.2"],
["A pension fund that has not yet moved to the new system has had a funding ratio that is too low for a long time. What measure can the fund take as a last resort?", [["Reducing pension entitlements and rights", "If recovery within the statutory periods fails, a fund can reduce pensions under strict conditions."], ["Temporarily suspending retirees' pensions", "Suspension of benefits is not a statutory instrument; the fund can, however, reduce."], ["Requiring participants to make a one-off additional payment", "Participants cannot be obliged to pay in extra to cover a fund's shortfall."], ["Forcing the employer to contribute the company to the fund", "The employer cannot be forced to contribute their company; reduction is the statutory last resort."]], "1h.2"],
["What is a characteristic disadvantage of a final-salary scheme for the employer or the fund compared with an average-salary scheme?", [["On a salary increase the pension over all past years of service must be raised", "In a final-salary scheme the last salary is the basis for all years, so a pay rise leads to expensive catch-up funding."], ["No partner's pension is accrued in a final-salary scheme", "Final-salary schemes too can include partner's pension; that is independent of the system."], ["In a final-salary scheme the employee bears the full investment risk on their contributions", "Investment risk lies with the participant in a contribution scheme, not in a final-salary scheme."], ["A final-salary scheme is not permitted for tax purposes", "Final-salary schemes were permitted within the Witteveen framework; the disadvantage is mainly financial."]], "1h.2"],
["Sophie (31) has just joined an architecture firm. On her payslip she sees that an own contribution to the pension scheme is withheld every month. Her employer pays the rest of the premium. Sophie asks whether she may deduct this own contribution in her income tax return. What is correct?", [["No, the contribution is already deducted from her taxable wages, so she pays no wage tax on it", "The employee contribution for a tax-compliant pension scheme directly reduces taxable wages; there is no second deduction."], ["Yes, she may deduct the contribution in her return as an expense for income provisions", "That deduction applies to annuity premium, not to the own contribution to occupational pension."], ["No, the contribution is taxed, but the later pension benefit is therefore untaxed", "The reverse-taxation rule works the other way round: the contribution is untaxed and the benefit taxed."], ["No, the contribution falls in box 3 as an asset and is exempt there", "Pension contributions do not fall in box 3."]], "1i.9"],
["Arend is 64 and has worked as a lorry driver for 25 years. The long driving is getting harder for him. He therefore wants to work two days a week less and cover that loss of income with his pension. His AOW age is still about three years away. What is generally correct?", [["Many schemes offer part-time pension: part of the pension starts and he continues working part of the time", "Part-time pension makes it possible to have part of the pension start earlier when working less."], ["That is not possible, because under the Pensions Act the old-age pension must always start in full at once", "Part-time pension is precisely possible in many schemes."], ["That is only possible if he also has his AOW start in part", "The AOW cannot start in part or earlier."], ["That is possible, but the part of the pension that has started must then be cashed in as a lump sum", "The part that has started is paid as a periodic benefit, not compulsorily cashed in."]], "1g.5"],
["What is the consequence for the level of the benefit if a participant has their old-age pension start earlier than the retirement date in the scheme?", [["The benefit becomes lower, because less has been accrued and it is paid out for longer", "Starting early is recalculated actuarially: fewer years of accrual and a longer payout period lead to a lower annual benefit."], ["The benefit stays the same, only the AOW becomes lower", "The AOW does not change; the supplementary pension that starts early is recalculated."], ["The benefit becomes higher, because the participant has worked for a shorter time and thus paid premiums for less time", "Working for a shorter time precisely means less accrual and thus a lower benefit."], ["A fine follows that the employee pays to the employer", "There is no fine; the effect lies entirely in the actuarial recalculation of the pension."]], "1g.5"],
["Hanneke (67) is retiring after a career as a hospital pharmacist. She is married to Karel, who as a self-employed person has accrued little pension of his own. Hanneke wants Karel to be well provided for if she dies first. Her own old-age pension is amply sufficient. Which choice can increase the survivor's pension for Karel?", [["Exchanging part of her old-age pension for additional partner's pension", "Through exchange her old-age pension becomes lower and the partner's pension for Karel higher."], ["A high-low construction, in which she receives a higher benefit in the first years", "A high-low construction changes the distribution over time of her own pension, not the partner's pension."], ["A lump sum of 10% of her pension on the retirement date", "A lump sum lowers her pension and does not increase the partner's pension."], ["Bringing forward the start date of her pension by a year", "Bringing it forward lowers her benefit and does not increase the partner's pension."]], "1g.13"],
["What does a high-low construction involve at the start of the old-age pension?", [["First a higher and then a lower benefit, within a statutory maximum ratio", "The tax rules limit the difference between the high and the low benefit; in this way sufficient pension remains for life."], ["The pension benefit rises annually by a fixed percentage", "A rising benefit is precisely the opposite; with high-low the benefit goes down after a period."], ["The partner first receives a high and later a low partner's pension", "High-low concerns the participant's old-age pension, not the partner's pension."], ["The participant is paid a high lump sum and then no periodic benefit any more", "A full payout as a lump sum is not high-low and is not permitted; the benefit remains lifelong."]], "1g.5"],
["Ronald (47) participated in a traditional contribution scheme with an insurer and had already accrued a substantial investment capital. The scheme did not include refund cover (restitutiedekking). Ronald dies suddenly. His brother, who is his only heir, asks the insurer to pay out the capital. What generally happens to the accrued capital in such a scheme?", [["It generally reverts to the provider or is used for survivor's pension", "Without refund cover the capital does not pay out to heirs; it is released or is used under the scheme for survivor's pension."], ["It is paid out in cash to the heirs under the statutory division or the will", "Payout to heirs precisely requires refund cover."], ["It is transferred to Ronald's employer", "The employer has no right to the pension capital."], ["It is compulsorily converted into an annuity (lijfrente) for the brother as heir", "There is no compulsory conversion into an annuity for heirs."]], "1i.8"],
["Bianca (45) is a team leader at a distribution centre and participates in her employer's pension scheme. After a serious back condition she is declared 80% incapacitated for work after two years of illness. The scheme includes premium waiver in case of incapacity for work. She asks what that means for her pension. What is correct?", [["Her accrual continues without premium having to be paid for the incapacitated part", "With premium waiver the provider takes over the premium for the incapacitated part, so that accrual continues."], ["She receives a lifelong supplementary benefit from the provider to replace her lost salary", "That is an incapacity pension or WIA excess cover, not premium waiver."], ["Her pension accrual stops entirely until she has recovered", "Premium waiver precisely ensures that accrual continues."], ["She will no longer have to pay tax on her pension benefit later", "Premium waiver has no influence on the taxation of the benefit."]], "1i.4"],
["What is the purpose of a WIA gap or WIA excess insurance within an employment benefits package?", [["To top up the loss of income in case of incapacity for work that is not covered by the WIA", "The WIA covers only part of the salary and is capped; these insurances fill the gap or the part above the maximum daily wage."], ["To have the provider take over the pension premium as long as the employee is incapacitated for work", "That is what premium waiver in case of incapacity for work in the pension scheme does."], ["A benefit to surviving dependants on the death of the employee", "Death risk is covered by partner's pension, Anw gap pension or a term life insurance, not by a WIA insurance."], ["To increase the AOW in case of early incapacity for work", "The AOW is not increased by incapacity for work; this concerns topping up income before the AOW age."]], "1i.8"],
["What information must an employee in any case receive from the provider when participation ends, for example on leaving employment?", [["A statement of the accrued entitlements and information on the possibility of value transfer", "When participation ends, the former participant must know what they have accrued and what choices they have, such as value transfer."], ["A quote for an annuity (lijfrente) from another provider into which the accrued pension can be paid", "The provider does not have to supply a third-pillar quote; it informs about the accrued pension."], ["An automatic cash-in sum for the accrued pension", "Leaving employment gives no right to cash in; the pension remains paid-up or is transferred through value transfer."], ["An overview of AOW accrual over the period of service", "AOW accrual is a matter for the SVB (Dutch Social Insurance Bank), not for the pension provider."]], "1h.16"],
["What does the move to defined contribution agreements only under the Wtp mean for the employer?", [["They pay an agreed premium in advance and have no obligation to top up shortfalls", "In a defined contribution agreement the employer's obligation is limited to the premium; an obligation to make additional payments in case of shortfalls does not fit that."], ["They will from now on guarantee a fixed benefit on the retirement date", "A guaranteed benefit belongs to a defined benefit agreement; that is precisely disappearing for new accrual."], ["They must adjust the premium every year to the funding ratio", "In the new system a stable premium is the starting point; the funding ratio as a steering instrument disappears."], ["They will from now on bear the full investment risk on the pension assets of all participants", "In a contribution scheme the investment risk lies with the participants, possibly shared collectively."]], "1f.2"],
["Who draws up the transition plan for an employer's scheme in the transition to the new pension system?", [["The employer, together with the employees or their representatives (social partners)", "In the transition plan the social partners lay down the new scheme, the choice on invaren and the compensation."], ["The AFM, as supervisor of pension communication and the implementation of pension schemes", "The AFM supervises information, but does not draw up plans for individual schemes."], ["The SVB, because it carries out the AOW", "The SVB has no role in the transition of supplementary pension."], ["Each participant individually, through a personal choice", "The transition is a collective process; participants do not draw up their own transition plan."]], "1h.13"],
["What is the role of the implementation plan in the transition to the new system?", [["In it the provider describes how it implements the new scheme and the transition", "The implementation plan follows the social partners' transition plan and shows how the provider fills in the agreements in practice."], ["In it participants individually choose whether they want to transfer their accrued pension (invaren)", "There is no individual choice on invaren; the decision is taken collectively."], ["In it the Tax and Customs Administration lays down the new tax limits", "The tax limits are in the law; the implementation plan is a document of the provider."], ["In it the AOW age is set for the participants", "The AOW age is determined by law, independently of the pension transition."]], "1h.13"],
["Does a participant in a solidarity contribution scheme have their own personal pension assets?", [["Yes, every participant is allocated pension assets, while investment is collective", "In the solidarity scheme too there are allocated pension assets per participant; the return is distributed through a collective allocation system."], ["No, there is only a collective pot without any allocation of assets to individual participants", "The new system precisely makes the assets per participant visible, also in the solidarity variant."], ["No, the participant accrues an entitlement to a fixed benefit", "A fixed benefit entitlement belongs to the old system; in a contribution scheme there are pension assets."], ["Yes, and they may invest those assets freely themselves", "Free individual investment choices fit the flexible scheme, not the collectively invested solidarity scheme."]], "1f.3"],
["What is the purpose of the protection return (beschermingsrendement) in the solidarity contribution scheme?", [["To protect the pensions of older participants in particular against fluctuations caused by interest rate changes", "The protection return moves with the interest rate, so that the expected benefit for participants close to retirement is more stable."], ["To provide a guaranteed minimum benefit to all participants, regardless of investment results", "The new system has no guarantees; the protection return only dampens interest rate risk."], ["To protect the employer against premium increases", "The protection return concerns the allocation of return to participants, not the level of the premium."], ["To protect young people against a premium that is too low", "The protection return is mainly aimed at participants closer to or in the payout phase."]], "1f.3"],
["What is a periodic risk preference survey (risicopreferentieonderzoek) at a pension provider for?", [["To establish participants' risk attitude, so that the investment policy fits it", "In the new system the policy must fit the participants' risk appetite; this is investigated periodically."], ["To assess participants' health for the premium of partner's pension on a risk basis", "Medical selection is not permitted; the survey concerns risk appetite in investing."], ["To determine which participants may opt for cashing in", "Cashing in is limited by law and is not determined by a risk preference survey."], ["To set the premium for each participant individually", "The premium is laid down in the scheme and is not determined per participant on the basis of risk attitude."]], "1f.1"],
["Hans (58) participates in a flexible contribution scheme under the Pension Transition Act. He has never looked at the investment options his provider offers. Now that his retirement is getting closer, he is worried about price falls. He asks how his pension assets are invested if he chooses nothing himself. What is correct?", [["According to the default lifecycle, in which the risk decreases as the retirement date approaches", "Without a choice of their own, assets are invested according to the default lifecycle, which reduces risk towards the retirement date."], ["It is invested entirely in shares until the retirement date", "A lifecycle precisely reduces risk; entirely shares until the end does not fit that."], ["It stays uninvested in a savings account until he makes a choice", "In a contribution scheme the assets are invested, even without a choice of one's own."], ["It is automatically transferred to the solidarity scheme because he made no choice", "Not choosing an investment profile does not lead to a different type of scheme."]], "1f.1"],
["What is a characteristic of the solidarity reserve in the solidarity contribution scheme?", [["It is filled from premium or excess return and can cushion setbacks", "The reserve shares risks between generations: in good times it is filled, in bad times it can be called on."], ["It is a personal savings pot that is paid out as an extra amount on retirement", "The reserve is collective and is not allocated to individual participants."], ["It is filled by a mandatory contribution from the AOW", "The AOW is separate from supplementary pension and contributes nothing to a solidarity reserve."], ["It guarantees that pensions can never fall", "The reserve dampens fluctuations, but offers no guarantee against reduction."]], "1f.3"],
["A pension provider starts using a new mortality table in which expected longevity is higher than in the old table. What is the general consequence?", [["Required provisions and purchasing lifelong benefits become more expensive", "If participants are expected to live longer, benefits must be paid for longer and more assets are needed."], ["The provisions fall, because fewer participants die before their retirement date", "Higher life expectancy raises the cost of lifelong benefits on balance."], ["There is no consequence, because mortality tables are only used for the AOW", "Mortality tables are precisely an important basis for supplementary pension."], ["The benefits are automatically increased by the extra years of life", "A new table raises the cost, not automatically the level of the benefit."]], "1h.22"],
["What is the pension base (pensioengrondslag) in a pension scheme?", [["Pensionable salary minus the offset (franchise)", "Pension or premium is calculated on the pension base; the offset takes the AOW into account."], ["The full gross salary including all allowances", "Not all salary components are pensionable and the offset is deducted."], ["The amount the employee pays themselves as premium", "The own contribution is part of the premium, not the base on which pension is accrued."], ["The net salary after payroll tax", "Pension is calculated on a gross base, not on net salary."]], "1h.3"],
["What is meant by a non-compliant act (onzuivere handeling) with a pension entitlement, such as cashing in outside the statutory exceptions?", [["An act contrary to the tax conditions, as a result of which the value is taxed as wages", "With a non-compliant act the tax facilitation lapses retroactively; the value is therefore taxed and revision interest applies."], ["An act that only affects the level of the premium in the following calendar year", "The consequences are much heavier: the full value of the entitlement is taxed."], ["An act in which the provider makes a calculation error", "The concept concerns tax-impermissible use of the entitlement, not administrative errors."], ["An act that only has criminal-law consequences", "The consequence is fiscal: levying on the value, not primarily a criminal-law sanction."]], "1j.5"],
["How high is the revision interest (revisierente) that can be levied in the case of a non-compliant act with a pension or annuity (lijfrente) entitlement?", [["20% of the value of the entitlement, with exceptions", "Revision interest compensates for the tax advantage obtained in the past and in principle amounts to 20%."], ["10% of the value of the entitlement", "You may know 10% from the maximum lump sum at the start of pension, not from revision interest."], ["52% of the value of the entitlement", "52% is the rate of, among others, the pseudo final levy on an early retirement scheme (RVU), not revision interest."], ["A fixed amount per year that the entitlement existed", "Revision interest is a percentage of the value, not a fixed amount per year."]], "1j.5"],
["How is the employer's premium for a tax-compliant pension scheme treated for the employee?", [["The premium does not form part of the employee's taxable wages", "Because of the reverse-taxation rule the entitlement is exempt; tax follows only on the benefit."], ["The premium is taxed as wages in kind in box 1", "That only happens with an excessive or non-compliant scheme, not with a scheme within the Witteveen framework."], ["The premium falls in box 3 as an asset for the employee", "Pension entitlements are not box 3 assets; they fall under the reverse-taxation rule in the wage sphere."], ["The employee may deduct the employer's premium in their return", "The employee does not pay this premium themselves and therefore cannot deduct it."]], "1g.10"],
["Someone receives an old-age pension from a pension fund. How is that benefit classified for tax purposes?", [["As wages from a former employment, taxed in box 1", "Pension is deferred wages; the provider withholds wage tax and the benefit falls in box 1."], ["As income from a substantial interest in box 2", "Box 2 concerns benefits from a substantial interest, such as dividend from one's own BV."], ["As a benefit from savings and investments in box 3", "Box 3 taxes assets; periodic pension benefits fall in box 1."], ["As an untaxed benefit because the premium had already been taxed", "That applies to net pension; with an ordinary scheme the premium was precisely untaxed."]], "1g.10"],
["What role does the pension accrual (pensioenaangroei, factor A) play in the tax margin for annuities (lijfrente)?", [["The pension accrual over the previous year reduces the annual margin (jaarruimte)", "Anyone who already accrues pension through the employer needs less tax room; factor A is therefore included in the annual margin calculation."], ["The pension accrual increases the annual margin", "More occupational pension precisely means a smaller pension shortfall and thus less annual margin."], ["Factor A determines the level of the AOW", "The AOW depends on years of residence and living situation, not on factor A."], ["Factor A applies only to the reservation margin of self-employed persons", "Factor A is precisely relevant for employees who accrue pension and reduces their annual margin."]], "1g.10"],
["What requirement applies to a general pension fund (APF) before it may carry out pension schemes?", [["It must hold a licence from DNB", "An APF may only carry out pension schemes once DNB has granted a licence."], ["It must have been declared mandatory for an industry by the minister", "Mandatory participation belongs to an industry-wide pension fund, not to an APF."], ["It must have been established as a public limited company with shareholders", "A pension fund, an APF too, is a foundation."], ["It must be registered with the AFM as a financial adviser", "An APF is a pension provider and not an adviser."]], "1h.23"],
["Mustafa (45) has a sole proprietorship as an installer and is an entrepreneur for income tax. He has never worked for an employer and accrues no pension. His adviser wants to calculate how much annuity (lijfrente) premium he can deduct within the annual margin. For that his premium base is needed. What counts towards Mustafa's premium base?", [["Among other things his profit from business, in addition to any wages or results from other activities", "The premium base consists of, among other things, profit from business, wages and results from other activities."], ["Only wages from employment, so an entrepreneur has no annual margin", "Entrepreneurs too have an annual margin; their profit counts."], ["His savings and investments in box 3", "Assets in box 3 do not count towards the premium base."], ["Only the dividend he receives from a substantial interest in box 2", "Income from a substantial interest does not count towards the premium base."]], "1g.10"],
["Monique (44) works for an employer that has introduced a new contribution scheme under the Pension Transition Act. She lives with her partner and has two young children. In the scheme the partner's pension before the retirement date is insured on a risk basis. Monique asks what the maximum tax-permitted level of that partner's pension is. What is correct?", [["At most 50% of pensionable salary", "Under the Wtp, partner's pension on a risk basis before the retirement date is limited for tax purposes to 50% of pensionable salary."], ["At most 70% of the old-age pension she would accrue if she kept working until the retirement date", "The link to 70% of the old-age pension belongs to partner's pension that starts after the retirement date, not to risk cover before that date."], ["At most 100% of pensionable salary", "Such a high partner's pension does not fit within the tax framework."], ["No tax limit applies, because it is a risk cover", "Tax maxima apply to partner's pension on a risk basis too."]], "1i.5"],
["Saskia has an annuity policy (lijfrenteverzekering) that will soon expire. She wants to use the capital for a benefit with another provider. Can that be done without tax consequences?", [["Yes, she can transfer the capital directly to another permitted provider", "A direct transfer between permitted providers is not cashing in; in this way Saskia can look for the best payout rate."], ["No, the benefit must always be purchased from the insurer with whom she accrued", "There is no obligation to stay with the same provider; transfer to another provider is permitted."], ["Only if she first has the capital paid into her own account", "Payment to Saskia herself would be taxed as cashing in; the transfer must take place directly."], ["Yes, but then the capital is taxed in box 3", "With a correct transfer the capital remains in the annuity sphere and exempt in box 3."]], "1g.10"],
["What does relinquishing (prijsgeven) a pension entitlement involve, and what is the tax consequence?", [["Giving up (part of) the entitlement, which as a non-compliant act can lead to taxation", "Relinquishing is giving up an entitlement in whole or in part; for tax purposes this is in principle treated as a non-compliant act."], ["Transferring the entitlement to another provider through value transfer, without any tax consequences", "Value transfer is not relinquishing; the entitlement is retained."], ["Temporarily making accrual paid-up during parental leave", "Interrupting accrual is not giving up entitlements already accrued."], ["Converting partner's pension into old-age pension on retirement, taxed as wages", "Exchange within the rules is a permitted choice and not relinquishing."]], "1j.5"],
["Why must a dga with a majority interest in their BV pay special attention to the risk of incapacity for work?", [["Because they are generally not compulsorily insured under the WIA and must make a provision themselves", "A dga who cannot be dismissed against their will is usually not insured for the employee insurance schemes."], ["Because their AOW lapses if they become incapacitated for work before their AOW age", "Incapacity for work has no influence on the entitlement to AOW."], ["Because their BV must by law be liquidated on their incapacity for work", "There is no obligation to liquidate a BV on the dga's incapacity for work."], ["Because the UWV (Employee Insurance Agency) sets a higher WIA benefit for dga's that the BV must repay", "No such arrangement exists; a dga usually has no entitlement to the WIA at all."]], "1j.15"],
["Ruud (52) is the dga of a consultancy and his BV has a lot of free liquidity. He still has annual margin left for an annuity (lijfrente). Ruud wants to have the annuity built up in his own BV, so that the money stays within his business. His bookkeeper doubts whether that is possible for tax purposes. Is this possible?", [["No, only a permitted insurer, bank or investment institution may offer a tax annuity", "The tax annuity must be placed with a provider named in the law; Ruud's own BV is not one of them."], ["Yes, if the BV has sufficient assets to pay out the annuity later", "The BV's assets are not decisive; the BV is not a permitted provider."], ["Yes, provided the annuity is included as a separate liability in the BV's annual accounts", "A mention in the annual accounts does not make the BV a permitted annuity provider."], ["Only if his partner gives written consent to the accrual in the BV", "The partner's consent changes nothing about the requirements for the provider."]], "1j.20"],
["Gert has a restaurant with a pension scheme with an insurer; no mandatory participation or collective labour agreement (cao) applies. His new cook Sven (26) does not want to participate because he prefers to keep more net pay now. Gert is willing to agree, but is unsure about the consequences. Later Sven or his partner could claim that he was never properly informed. What should the adviser point out to Gert?", [["That he should record the information given and Sven's choice in writing, to prevent later claims", "When someone opts out of participation, a signed statement explaining the consequences is important to limit liability."], ["That an oral agreement suffices, because Sven can never bring a claim later", "Without a written record Gert will find it hard to prove that Sven was properly informed."], ["That he is legally obliged to pay Sven the full premium amount as extra gross salary", "There is no legal obligation to pay out the premium as wages."], ["That Sven automatically participates again as soon as he gets a partner", "There is no automatic participation on getting a partner."]], "1i.2"],
["Iris (38) is a lawyer at a bank and accrues pension through her employer up to the cap. Her salary is well above it. Her employer does not offer net pension. Iris still wants to save extra for her old age on income above the cap. Which third-pillar option can fit her situation?", [["A net annuity (nettolijfrente), with contributions from net income and a box 3 exemption during accrual", "The net annuity is intended for those who earn above the cap and cannot accrue net pension."], ["An annuity whose premium is deductible on the whole income above the cap", "Above the cap there is precisely no tax deduction for old-age accrual."], ["A second occupational pension with a provider of her choice, alongside her employer's scheme", "An employee cannot take out a second occupational pension themselves."], ["An increase of her AOW by voluntarily paying extra AOW premium", "The AOW cannot be raised above full accrual by extra premium."]], "1g.10"],
["Jan (64) and Petra (63) are divorcing after thirty years of marriage. Jan worked full time all those years, Petra largely looked after the children and worked little. Jan's old-age pension is equalised under the Wvps. Petra asks whether she is also entitled to part of Jan's AOW. What is correct?", [["No, the AOW is not equalised; each partner accrues their own AOW", "The AOW is a national insurance scheme for which each person accrues their own right; the Wvps concerns only supplementary old-age pension."], ["Yes, she is entitled to half of the AOW that Jan accrued during the marriage", "The AOW is not equalised."], ["Yes, but only if Petra herself has accrued less AOW than Jan", "Even then the AOW is not covered by equalisation."], ["Only if they include the division of the AOW in the divorce covenant", "The AOW is a personal right that cannot be divided through a covenant."]], "1h.18"],
["Does the Pensions (Division on Divorce) Act (Wvps) also apply to legal separation (scheiding van tafel en bed)?", [["Yes, equalisation can also take place on legal separation", "Besides divorce and the ending of a registered partnership, the Wvps also mentions legal separation."], ["No, only on a pronounced divorce", "The law does not limit equalisation to divorce; legal separation falls under it too."], ["No, because the marriage continues to exist on legal separation", "Although the marriage formally continues, the community ends and equalisation can apply."], ["Only if the court orders it separately", "Equalisation follows from the law itself; a separate court order is not needed."]], "1h.18"],
["Erik (56) is the dga of a structural engineering consultancy. In his BV he still has a pension in own management (pensioen in eigen beheer) that he has left paid-up. Erik and his wife Ingrid are divorcing after 22 years of marriage. Erik believes his pension falls outside the division because it is in his own BV. Does the Wvps apply to this pension?", [["Yes, the Wvps also applies to pension in own management at the BV", "The Wvps makes no distinction by provider; pension in own management is also equalised."], ["No, the Wvps applies only to pension at a pension fund", "The Wvps applies to pension entitlements regardless of whether they are placed with a fund, insurer or own BV."], ["No, because the Pensions Act, and thus the Wvps too, does not apply to a dga and their BV", "The Wvps is a separate act that also applies to pension in own management."], ["Only if the BV made a profit in the years of the marriage", "The BV's profit is not decisive for the application of the Wvps."]], "1j.16"],
["When can conversion (conversie) of pension take place on divorce?", [["When both ex-partners agree to it and the pension provider cooperates", "Conversion gives the ex-partner their own right; this requires agreements between the parties and the provider's consent."], ["Automatically on every divorce, without the ex-partners having to agree anything", "The default is equalisation; conversion requires an explicit choice by the parties."], ["Only if the participant has already retired", "Conversion can precisely be agreed before the retirement date."], ["Only at the request of the participant's employer", "The employer is not a party to the division; it concerns the ex-partners and the provider."]], "1h.18"],
["Willem (54) and Saar (52) divorced two years ago. They reported the divorce to Willem's pension fund in time, so Saar is entitled to equalisation. Willem's pension scheme includes a partner's pension. Willem dies unexpectedly, well before his retirement date. What is Saar in principle entitled to?", [["The special partner's pension (bijzonder partnerpensioen), not part of Willem's old-age pension", "Because Willem dies before his retirement date, no old-age pension is paid out; Saar is, however, entitled to the special partner's pension."], ["Half of Willem's full old-age pension, payable from his retirement date", "Equalisation follows Willem's old-age pension; if he dies before the retirement date, it is not paid out."], ["An Anw benefit as Willem's divorced partner", "A divorced partner is not a surviving dependant within the meaning of the Anw."], ["Payment of the cash-in value of Willem's accrued pension", "Cashing in the pension for the ex-partner is not a consequence of death."]], "1h.18"],
["Which act regulates the division of pension on divorce in October 2026?", [["The Pensions (Division on Divorce) Act (Wvps)", "The Wvps has applied since 1995; the intended successor with conversion as the default has not been introduced."], ["A new act with conversion as the default, which has replaced the Wvps", "Such a successor has been proposed, but not introduced; the Wvps still applies."], ["The Pension Transition Act", "The Wtp reforms the pension system, but does not independently regulate the division on divorce."], ["Only matrimonial property law of the Dutch Civil Code", "A separate act applies to pension; matrimonial property law regulates other asset components."]], "1h.13"],
["Tom (40) and Mila (38) were married for ten years and are now divorcing. Tom is a photographer with his own business and built up an annuity policy (lijfrenteverzekering) during the marriage. Mila built up occupational pension in employment. They ask how Tom's annuity is to be divided. What is correct?", [["Through matrimonial property law (division or settlement), not through the Wvps", "An annuity is not pension within the meaning of the Wvps; the division follows from matrimonial property law and their agreements."], ["Through standard equalisation under the Wvps, carried out by the insurer", "The Wvps concerns old-age pension from occupational pension, not annuities."], ["Not at all; an annuity always remains entirely with the person who took out the policy", "An annuity can belong to the assets to be divided or settled."], ["By compulsorily cashing in the annuity and dividing the net proceeds equally", "There is no obligation to cash in; cashing in can in fact be tax-disadvantageous."]], "1h.18"],
["What is an important risk of a pension or retirement obligation (ODV) that has remained in the dga's own BV?", [["The payment depends on the BV's financial position, for example in case of bankruptcy", "In own management the assets are not ring-fenced; if the BV gets into difficulties, the entitlement can become worthless."], ["The entitlement falls under DNB's prudential supervision, just as is the case with a pension fund", "Own management does not fall under the prudential supervision that applies to pension funds."], ["The entitlement is taxed annually in box 3", "A pension or ODV entitlement falls under the reverse-taxation rule and not in box 3."], ["The entitlement lapses automatically on the sale of the BV", "On a sale the obligation must be arranged, but it does not lapse by itself."]], "1j.19"],
["A dga has their BV pay premium for an external pension scheme with an insurer. How is that premium treated for tax purposes at the BV?", [["As deductible costs within the tax limits of the Witteveen framework", "The premium is a remuneration component for the dga as employee; within the limits it is deductible for corporate income tax."], ["As a profit distribution to the dga, which is not deductible for the BV", "A compliant pension premium is employment remuneration, not a profit distribution."], ["As income from a substantial interest of the dga, taxed in box 2 on payout", "The premium is not treated as dividend; it falls under the reverse-taxation rule in the wage sphere."], ["As a gift to the dga", "There is no question of a gift; it concerns a pension promise in the context of the employment."]], "1j.20"],
["Marieke (60) is the dga of a clothing shop and has converted her pension in own management into a retirement obligation (ODV). The shop has been making losses for years and the BV has little assets left. Marieke counts on the ODV providing a fixed income from her AOW age. She asks her adviser whether she should be worried. What should the adviser point out to her?", [["That payment of the ODV is uncertain and she must look at her old-age provision more broadly", "An ODV is an obligation of the BV; if the BV has insufficient means, the payment is at risk."], ["That the ODV is guaranteed by the State if the BV cannot pay", "There is no State guarantee for an ODV."], ["That she can cash in the ODV at any time without tax or revision interest to secure the money", "Cashing in an ODV outside the rules is a non-compliant act with tax consequences."], ["That the ODV automatically transfers to a pension fund in case of losses", "An ODV does not automatically transfer to a pension fund."]], "1j.19"],
["What is a company pension fund (ondernemingspensioenfonds)?", [["A pension fund for one company or a group of affiliated companies", "A company pension fund is established for one employer or group; participation follows from the employment contract with that employer."], ["A fund that the minister has made mandatory for all employers in an industry", "That describes an industry-wide pension fund, not a company pension fund."], ["A fund in which only self-employed persons participate", "Self-employed persons do not participate in a company pension fund; it is linked to an employer."], ["An insurer that carries out only contribution schemes", "A company pension fund is a foundation, not an insurer, and is not limited to contribution schemes."]], "1g.8"],
["An employer joins, with its pension scheme, a collectivity circle of a general pension fund (APF). What risk does that entail?", [["In case of a shortfall in the circle, pensions in that circle can be reduced, independently of the other circles", "Each circle is financially separate and has its own financial position; setbacks stay within the circle."], ["In case of a shortfall in another circle, its circle must always contribute", "Circles are precisely separate from one another."], ["The employer becomes a co-owner of the APF and is liable for all circles", "Joining does not make the employer liable for other circles."], ["The circle can never be left again, not even through collective value transfer", "Switching to another provider is possible, for example through collective value transfer."]], "1g.12"],
["A participant has a complaint about how their pension is carried out at a pension fund and is dissatisfied after the internal complaints procedure. Where can they turn?", [["To the Pensions Ombudsman (Ombudsman Pensioenen)", "The Pensions Ombudsman handles complaints about pension funds; complaints about insurers and advisers go to Kifid (Dutch Financial Services Complaints Institute)."], ["To Kifid, for all complaints about pension funds", "Kifid handles complaints about financial service providers such as insurers and advisers, not about pension funds."], ["To the SVB (Dutch Social Insurance Bank), because it carries out the pensions", "The SVB carries out the AOW and Anw and handles no complaints about supplementary pension."], ["To DNB, which settles individual complaints", "DNB supervises prudentially but does not settle individual disputes."]], "1a.1"],
["Erwin owns a cleaning company with 30 employees. For years he has had a good pension scheme of his own with an insurer. It now turns out that his company falls under the mandatory participation of the industry-wide pension fund for his sector. He would like to keep his own scheme. What can Erwin do?", [["Apply, under conditions, for exemption from mandatory participation from the industry-wide pension fund", "The exemption rules make it possible under conditions to keep an own scheme; the application goes to the fund."], ["Ignore the mandatory participation, because he already has a pension scheme of his own", "Mandatory participation also applies if an own scheme exists; ignoring it can lead to premium claims."], ["Let the employees themselves choose which provider they want to participate in", "Mandatory participation allows no individual choice for employees."], ["Apply to the AFM for an exemption from mandatory participation", "The AFM does not grant exemption from mandatory participation."]], "1g.8"],
["A software company with 120 employees has had a pension scheme with an insurer for fifteen years. Director Annelies (51) wants to switch to a general pension fund (APF) from next year. She wants the pensions her employees have accrued with the insurer to go to the APF as well. In this way the employees do not have to keep track of multiple pensions. What is this transfer called?", [["Collective value transfer", "In a collective value transfer the accrued entitlements of a group of participants go to another provider at the same time."], ["Individual value transfer per participant", "Individual value transfer belongs to a change of job by a single employee."], ["Invaren", "Invaren is the conversion of existing entitlements to a new contribution scheme under the Wtp."], ["Conversion", "Conversion is a term from the division of pension on divorce."]], "1g.4"],
["What does a guarantee contract (garantiecontract) with a pension insurer involve?", [["The insurer guarantees the benefits and bears the investment and longevity risk", "With a guarantee contract the insurer stands behind the agreed benefits, regardless of the return."], ["The employer guarantees the employee a minimum return on the pension premiums paid", "With a guarantee contract it is precisely the insurer that guarantees, not the employer."], ["The AFM guarantees the pension in case of the insurer's bankruptcy", "The AFM is a conduct supervisor and gives no guarantees on pensions."], ["The participant is guaranteed to get their premiums paid back", "Refund of premium is a different cover; the guarantee contract concerns the benefits."]], "1g.11"],
["Peter (66) has a contribution scheme with an insurer and retires next year. He wants to convert his capital into a fixed lifelong benefit. The market interest rate has fallen sharply over the past year. The quote he now receives is therefore lower than a year ago. Why is that?", [["With a lower interest rate more capital is needed for the same benefit, so he buys less benefit", "An insurer calculates with the interest rate; with a low rate the capital is worth less in lifelong benefit."], ["With a falling interest rate the insurer may unilaterally double its costs", "The lower quote is due to the interest rate, not to a statutory cost increase."], ["The lower interest rate reduces his AOW, which is offset against the benefit", "The AOW does not depend on the market interest rate and is not offset."], ["The interest rate has no influence; the difference is only due to higher tax", "The interest rate is precisely an important factor in purchasing a benefit."]], "1h.15"],
["An adviser advises a client on an annuity policy (lijfrenteverzekering). How is the adviser remunerated for that advice?", [["The client pays them directly, because a commission ban applies to this product", "For complex financial products such as life and annuity policies the adviser may not receive commission from the provider."], ["The insurer pays them an acquisition commission, built into the premium", "Commission from the provider is precisely not permitted for this kind of product."], ["The Tax and Customs Administration reimburses the advice costs through the annual margin", "The Tax and Customs Administration does not pay advice costs; the client pays the adviser directly."], ["The client's employer always pays the advice costs", "With an individual annuity the employer is not a party; the client pays themselves."]], "4a.4"],
["A client is dissatisfied with the pension advice of their financial adviser and cannot resolve it with the firm. Where can they turn with their complaint?", [["To Kifid (Dutch Financial Services Complaints Institute)", "Financial service providers must be affiliated with Kifid, which handles consumers' complaints about advice."], ["To the Pensions Ombudsman (Ombudsman Pensioenen), which handles all pension complaints", "The Pensions Ombudsman handles complaints about pension funds, not about financial advisers."], ["To the SVB (Dutch Social Insurance Bank)", "The SVB carries out national insurance schemes and handles no complaints about advisers."], ["To the Dutch Data Protection Authority (AP)", "The AP concerns privacy; it handles no substantive complaints about financial advice."]], "1a.1"],
["After fifteen years Karin (48) moved from a healthcare institution to a municipality. Her old pension is paid-up at the healthcare pension fund, her new pension she accrues at the new employer's fund. She has received a letter about the possibility of value transfer. Karin asks her adviser whether she should have the old pension transferred. What belongs in any case to careful advice?", [["Comparing the schemes on, among other things, financial position, indexation, survivor cover and costs", "Value transfer can turn out advantageous or disadvantageous; that only becomes clear after comparing the main features of both schemes."], ["Always advising to transfer, because one pension with one provider is clearer for her", "Clarity is no good reason if the old scheme has better terms."], ["Advising to cash in the value and pay it into an annuity (lijfrente)", "Cashing in a pension is in principle not permitted and transfer to an annuity is not possible."], ["Looking only at the amount of the transfer value that the old fund states", "The amount of the value says little without comparing what she gets in return in the new scheme."]], "1h.4"],
["How must pension providers in principle supply their information to participants?", [["Electronically, unless the participant opts for information on paper", "The Pension Communication Act makes digital information the default, with a right to paper for those who want it."], ["Exclusively by post, to guarantee reachability", "Digital has precisely become the starting point; paper remains possible on request."], ["Exclusively through the employer, on the company's intranet", "The provider is itself responsible for the information and may not rely on the employer's intranet."], ["Only orally during a personal conversation", "Oral information is not sufficient; the law requires information that is recorded and accessible."]], "1g.13"],
["An installation company has a contribution scheme in which the premium is a fixed percentage of the pension base. Management expects to grow in the coming years from 50 to 70 employees with comparable salaries. What does that mean for pension costs?", [["Pension costs rise roughly in proportion to the sum of the pension bases", "With a fixed premium percentage, costs grow along with the number of participants and their pension base."], ["Pension costs stay the same, because the premium percentage does not change", "The same percentage over more bases gives higher total costs."], ["Pension costs fall through economies of scale to below the current level", "Economies of scale can lower costs somewhat, but the total rises with the growth."], ["The costs cannot be estimated, because they depend on the insurer's funding ratio", "With a contribution scheme the costs follow from the agreed premium."]], "1h.20"],
["Paul (61) works as a project manager at an engineering firm. He is healthy, but would like to stop working at 63 to spend more time with his grandchildren. His wife still works part time and has a small pension of her own. Paul asks his adviser whether he can afford to retire at 63. What must the adviser in any case map out?", [["The income before and after the AOW age, the effect of early retirement and net purchasing power", "With early retirement a period without AOW arises and the pension becomes lower; net disposable income is decisive."], ["Only the gross pension benefit at 63, as stated on his Uniform Pension Overview", "The gross pension says little without the AOW period, tax and the effect on the whole household."], ["Only the level of his AOW, because it determines his income", "The AOW is only one source and moreover starts later."], ["The possibility of having his AOW start already from 63", "The AOW cannot be brought forward."]], "1h.14"],
["A client says he never reads the pension letters from his fund because he finds them too complicated. Which approach best fits an adviser's duty of care?", [["Going through the essentials together in comprehensible language and explaining the choices and risks to him", "A good adviser aligns with the client's level of knowledge and makes the essentials of pension information understandable."], ["Advising him to ignore the letters, because his pension through the employer is well arranged anyway", "That leaves the client ignorant about choices and risks; this does not fit careful service."], ["Referring him to the AFM for an explanation of his scheme", "The AFM does not give individual explanations of pension schemes."], ["Answering the letters on his behalf without consulting him", "Acting without consultation does not fit an advisory relationship; the client must be able to make a considered choice himself."]], "2j.4"],
["Henk dies at the age of 68. He had remarried Ans, who now receives partner's pension from Henk's pension fund. Henk has two children from his first marriage. They think the partner's pension belongs to the estate and want their share. What is correct?", [["The partner's pension is Ans's own right and does not fall into the estate", "Partner's pension is a direct right of the surviving partner against the provider and does not belong to the estate."], ["The partner's pension falls into the estate and is divided according to the will", "The partner's pension does not belong to the estate."], ["The children can calculate their statutory share (legitieme portie) on the present value of the partner's pension", "Because the partner's pension is not part of the estate, it does not count towards the statutory share."], ["The pension fund divides the partner's pension equally between Ans and all the children", "The partner's pension is for the partner; children can at most have an orphan's pension of their own."]], "1h.16"],
["Lars (57) was dismissed after 28 years in a reorganisation and has no new job yet. He receives a WW (unemployment) benefit. Lars wants to prevent his pension accrual from stalling, because he is already getting on in years. He asks whether he can continue accrual at his old pension fund. What is generally possible?", [["Voluntary continuation for a limited period, if the regulations allow it and he pays the premium himself", "Many schemes allow voluntary continuation after dismissal; the participant then pays themselves and the duration is limited for tax purposes."], ["Unlimited continuation until his AOW age, with the old employer simply continuing to pay the full premium", "There is no unlimited continuation and the old employer no longer pays after the employment ends."], ["Continuation through the WW, with the UWV (Employee Insurance Agency) automatically taking over the full pension premium", "The UWV does not automatically take over the pension premium during the WW."], ["No possibility at all, because his entitlements are cashed in immediately on dismissal", "Accrued entitlements remain paid-up and are not simply cashed in."]], "1h.16"],
["What are pension regulations (pensioenreglement)?", [["The provider's document in which the rights and obligations of participants under the scheme are laid down", "The regulations elaborate the pension agreement and determine, among other things, who is a partner, what choices there are and how the pension is calculated."], ["The statutory regulation in which the government determines the level of all supplementary pensions", "The government does not determine the level of supplementary pension; it follows from the agreements of employer and employees."], ["The annual overview of accrued entitlements that every participant receives from the provider", "That is the Uniform Pension Overview; the regulations contain the rules of the pension scheme itself."], ["The agreement between employer and provider on premium payment and the services to be delivered", "That is the implementation agreement; the regulations govern the relationship between provider and participant."]], "1i.1"]
];
